    {"id": "V3-doc03_p027_c001", "title": "The HS Codes below will be replaced on Saber Platform starting 2025-06-01 (ZATCA", "content": "The HS Codes below will be replaced on Saber Platform starting 2025-06-01 (ZATCA update). 730711000001 -> 730711000000: Couplings of non-malleable cast iron – وصالت من حديد صب غير قابل للطرق. 730711000002 -> 730711000000: Elbows of non-malleable cast iron – أكواع. 730711000003 -> 730711000000: Sleeves – أكمام. 730711009999 -> 730711000000: Other tube or pipe fittings. 841311000001 -> 841311000000: Pumps for dispensing fuel – مضخات توزيع الوقود. 841311000002 -> 841311000000: Pumps for dispensing lubricants – مضخات توزيع مواد التشحيم. 910212000001 -> 910212000000: Wrist-watches with electronic d", "source": "hscodes-1-2026.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc03_p028_c001", "title": "HS codes updated on Saber Platform (17-03-2025). 731300000000 – Barbed wire of i", "content": "HS codes updated on Saber Platform (17-03-2025). 731300000000 – Barbed wire of iron/steel for fencing – أسلاك شائكة من حديد أو صلب للسياج – Technical Regulation for Building Materials Part 1. 731412000000 – Endless bands for machinery of stainless steel – أشرطة مقلقة بدون نهايات للآلات من صلب مقاوم للصدأ. 731414000000 – Other woven cloth of stainless steel. 731419000000 – Other. 731420000000 – Grill, netting welded at intersection, wire ≥3mm, mesh ≥100cm² – شباك وسياج شبكية ملحومة عند نقاط التقاطع. 731431000001 – Covered with zinc – مغطاة بالزنك.", "source": "hscodes-1-2026.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc03_p030_c001", "title": "731700900000 – Other – غيرها. 731813000002 – Nails with ring heads – براغي برؤوس", "content": "731700900000 – Other – غيرها. 731813000002 – Nails with ring heads – براغي برؤوس حلقية. 741510000001 – Nails – مسامير. 741510000002 – Upholstery nails – مسامير نتيجيد. 741510009999 – Other. 750890300001 – Nickel screws – مسامير من نيكل. 761610000001 – Aluminum screws – مسامير من ألومنيوم. 790700500000 – Nails, tacks, nuts, bolts, screws – مسامير (قالوزو) ومسامير النتيجيد والصواميل والمسامير الملولبة. 853080009999 – Other equipment – غيرها من أجهزة أخر – Technical Regulation for Telecommunications Devices. 853010000000 – Equipment for railways or tramways – أجهزة للطرق الحديدية أو الترام. 88079", "source": "hscodes-1-2026.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc04_p011_c001", "title": "Data subject rights under PDPL: 1) Right to be informed (Art.4(1)); 2) Right to ", "content": "Data subject rights under PDPL: 1) Right to be informed (Art.4(1)); 2) Right to access personal data (Art.4(2)); 3) Right to obtain personal data in readable/clear format (Art.4(3)); 4) Right to correct/complete/update personal data (Art.4(4)); 5) Right to request destruction (Art.4(5)); 6) Right to withdraw consent (Art.5(2)); 7) Right to submit complaint to Competent Authority (Art.34). Controller must respond within 30 days, extendable by another 30 days if disproportionate effort or multiple requests.", "source": "ksa-personal-data-protection-law-series-part-1.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p001_c001", "title": "Saudi Standards, Metrology and Quality Organization SASO. Technical Regulation f", "content": "Saudi Standards, Metrology and Quality Organization SASO. Technical Regulation for Leather Products. Approved in SASO Board of Directors meeting No. (179) on 15/06/1442 AH (28/01/2021). Published in Official Gazette on 29/11/1442 AH (07/09/2021 AD). Version (1). Note: Only Arabic version is authentic in law.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p002_c001", "title": "Contents: Article (1) Terms and Definitions; (2) Scope; (3) Objectives; (4) Obli", "content": "Contents: Article (1) Terms and Definitions; (2) Scope; (3) Objectives; (4) Obligations of Supplier; (5) Labeling; (6) Conformity Assessment Procedures; (7) Responsibilities of Regulatory Authorities; (8) Market Surveillance Authorities; (9) Violations and Penalties; (10) General Provisions; (11) Transitional Provisions; (12) Publication; plus Annexes 1A, 1B, 2, 3, 4.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p003_c001", "title": "Preamble: In line with KSA accession to WTO (Decree No.244), SASO issued this Te", "content": "Preamble: In line with KSA accession to WTO (Decree No.244), SASO issued this Technical Regulation based on Statute Articles 3,4,6. Technical regulation includes essential requirements and conformity assessment procedures. All public and private sectors shall adhere to Saudi standards.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p004_c001", "title": "Article (1) Terms and Definitions: KSA, Board, SASO, Regulatory Authorities, Mar", "content": "Article (1) Terms and Definitions: KSA, Board, SASO, Regulatory Authorities, Market Surveillance Authorities, Technical Regulation, Standard, Essential Requirements, Hazard(s), Risk(s), Supplier (manufacturer resident in KSA, or agent if manufacturer outside KSA, or importer if no agent), Conformity Assessment Procedures, Notified Bodies, Certificate of Conformity, Supplier Declaration of Conformity, Saudi Quality Mark, Placing on Market, Making Available on Market, Withdrawal, Recall, Product, Tanning, Articles of Leather Products, Label.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p005_c001", "title": "Article (1) continued: Tanning definition, Articles of Leather Products definiti", "content": "Article (1) continued: Tanning definition, Articles of Leather Products definition (articles that contain natural leather or synthetic leather except footwear). Label definition: information shown on product as specified in relevant standard.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p006_c001", "title": "Article (2) Scope: Applies to all leather products (natural or synthetic or mixt", "content": "Article (2) Scope: Applies to all leather products (natural or synthetic or mixture) and their articles. Exceptions: footwear (covered by separate Technical Regulation of Footwear), animal hides pre-tanning (raw materials for manufacturing).", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p006_c002", "title": "Article (3) Objectives: Lay out essential requirements, identify conformity asse", "content": "Article (3) Objectives: Lay out essential requirements, identify conformity assessment procedures suppliers must comply with when placing products in KSA markets, to ensure product conformity to basic requirements for environment, health and consumer safety.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p006_c003", "title": "Article (4) Obligations of Supplier: 4/1 General Requirements: A) Compliance wit", "content": "Article (4) Obligations of Supplier: 4/1 General Requirements: A) Compliance with essential requirements, provide documentation upon request. B) Meet technical requirements in this regulation and relevant standards. C) Provide information on potential health risks. D) Comply with labelling. E) Required conformity assessment. F) Effective environmental management system (ISO 14001 considered sufficient).", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p007_c001", "title": "4/2 Requirements Related to Animal Hides: Prohibited to trade/display leather of", "content": "4/2 Requirements Related to Animal Hides: Prohibited to trade/display leather of endangered animals protected by international agreements. Prohibited to use leather of forbidden animals, animal source must be mentioned. Harmful substances must comply with permissible limits in relevant standards (chromium VI, aromatic amine, formaldehyde, chlorophenol). Pigments/dyes shall not contain cleavable arylamines, carcinogenic/allergenic dyes, flame-retardant dyes. Avoid low-biodegradable compounds like Ethylenediaminetriacetate.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p007_c002", "title": "4/4 Metrological Requirements: Use SI units or multiples/parts thereof. 4/5 Pack", "content": "4/4 Metrological Requirements: Use SI units or multiples/parts thereof. 4/5 Packaging Requirements: Appropriate packaging, according to product nature and relevant standard.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p008_c001", "title": "Article (5) Labeling: Label must include: a) supplier name and commercial regist", "content": "Article (5) Labeling: Label must include: a) supplier name and commercial registration, b) country of origin, c) product name and type, d) warnings and precautions, e) safety instructions, f) classification of product (e.g. safety/professional footwear for PPE regulation). Data must be in Arabic or Arabic+English. Label must be firmly fixed, difficult to remove, contain correct/proven information. Images/phrases shall not violate Islamic values.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p008_c002", "title": "Article (6) Conformity Assessment Procedures: 6/1 Only requirements of this tech", "content": "Article (6) Conformity Assessment Procedures: 6/1 Only requirements of this technical regulation must be met. 6/2 Supplier must obtain CoC from notified body: Type 3 for certain products (as shown in Annex 2), Type 1a for others (Annex 3). 6/3 Notified body carries out assessment. 6/4 Technical file includes: Supplier Declaration of Conformity (Annex 4), risk assessment, country of origin, test reports, list of standards, product explanatory booklet if label cannot be affixed. 6/5 Products with Saudi Quality Mark are deemed compliant.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p009_c001", "title": "Article (7) Responsibilities of Regulatory Authorities: Verify products fulfill ", "content": "Article (7) Responsibilities of Regulatory Authorities: Verify products fulfill conformity assessment procedures and technical documents; randomly sample products and refer to laboratories; charge suppliers with testing costs; withdraw non-conforming products and take legal actions.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p009_c002", "title": "Article (8) Responsibilities of Market Surveillance Authorities: Enforce market ", "content": "Article (8) Responsibilities of Market Surveillance Authorities: Enforce market surveillance on products in markets and warehouses; take samples to conduct necessary tests; in case of non-conformity, take administrative actions including withdrawal and recall.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p010_c001", "title": "Article (9) Violations and Penalties: Prohibited to manufacture/import/launch/ad", "content": "Article (9) Violations and Penalties: Prohibited to manufacture/import/launch/advertise non-conforming products. Non-conformity includes: improper fixing of labels/marks, failure to issue CoC, incomplete technical documentation, missing product data. Actions: mandate withdrawal, destroy or export products, withdraw/restrain/destroy, announce recall. SASO may cancel CoC and take measures with notified body. Penalties per Anti-Commercial Fraud Law.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p011_c001", "title": "Article (10) General Provisions: Supplier bears full legal responsibility. Must ", "content": "Article (10) General Provisions: Supplier bears full legal responsibility. Must comply with other applicable systems (trading, transport, storage, environment, security, safety). Provide inspectors with information/facilities. Disputes referred to SASO committee. Supplier may resubmit after corrections, bearing additional expenses. SASO may cancel CoC/Q-Mark. Modifications to product during validity annul certificate. SASO exclusively interprets the regulation.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p012_c001", "title": "Article (11) Transitional Provisions: Supplier has 180 days from publication to ", "content": "Article (11) Transitional Provisions: Supplier has 180 days from publication to take corrective actions. Non-complying products may be traded for up to 365 days from publication. This regulation supersedes preceding regulations in its scope. Article (12) Publication: to be published in Official Gazette.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p013_c001", "title": "Annex (1-A) List of Standards: SASO-ISO-17234-1 (azo colorants), SASO-ISO-17072-", "content": "Annex (1-A) List of Standards: SASO-ISO-17234-1 (azo colorants), SASO-ISO-17072-1/2 (mineral content), SASO-ISO-17070 (pentachlorophenol), SASO-ISO-17075-1/2 (chromium VI), SASO-ISO-17226-1/2 (formaldehyde), SASO-ISO-5431/5432/5433 (aqua sheep/lamb/cow hides), SASO-ISO-11646 (area measurement), SASO-GSO-2440 (general requirements), SASO-ASTM-D3136 (care label terminology), SASO-GSO-1956 (harmful substances), SASO-ISO-17076-1 (abrasion resistance), SASO-ISO-10195 (thermal aging/hexavalent chromium), SASO-ISO-11644 (adhesive strength), SASO-ISO-4045/2589 (pH), SASO-ISO-3376 (tensile strength), S", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p014_c001", "title": "Note: List of standards is subject to review; suppliers must use latest standard", "content": "Note: List of standards is subject to review; suppliers must use latest standards via SASO website.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p015_c001", "title": "Annex (1-B) List of Products and Customs Coding (HS Codes): 4104 (tanned bovine/", "content": "Annex (1-B) List of Products and Customs Coding (HS Codes): 4104 (tanned bovine/equine), 4105 (tanned sheep/lamb), 4106 (other animals), 4107 (leather further prepared bovine/equine), 4112 (sheep/lamb), 4113 (other animals), 4114 (chamois/patent/metallized), 4115 (composition leather), 4201 (saddlery), 4202 (luggage), 4203 (apparel of leather), 4205 (other articles), 4206 (articles of gut), 4301 (raw furskins), 4302 (tanned/dressed furskins), 4303 (apparel of fur), 6506 (headgear), 9113 (watch straps). Note: Saber electronic platform has updated/approved codes.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p016_c001", "title": "Annex (2) Conformity Assessment Form (Type 3) – Type Approval Based on Quality A", "content": "Annex (2) Conformity Assessment Form (Type 3) – Type Approval Based on Quality Assurance of Production Process. 1) Type Approval: supplier fulfills obligations, ensures products conform to approved type and technical regulations. 2) Manufacturing: certified Product Safety Management System required, subject to periodic surveillance. 3) Product Safety Management System: supplier submits request to Notified Body including name/address, license, declaration, product info, system documentation, technical documents. System must guarantee conformity.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p017_c001", "title": "3/3 System documentation must include: quality objectives, organizational struct", "content": "3/3 System documentation must include: quality objectives, organizational structure, manufacturing techniques, inspections and tests, records (test/calibration reports, personnel qualifications), control means. 3/4 Notified Body assesses system for 3 years. 3/5 Product presumed compliant if conforming to standards. 3/6 Auditing team must have technical expert experienced in product safety and manufacturing. 3/7 Audit includes factory visit. 3/8 Manufacturer notified of decision with justifications. 3/9 Manufacturer must maintain system. 3/10 Manufacturer notifies Body of proposed modifications", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p018_c001", "title": "4 Periodic Surveillance: Body verifies supplier meets obligations; supplier allo", "content": "4 Periodic Surveillance: Body verifies supplier meets obligations; supplier allows access to manufacturing/inspection/testing/storage sites; Body carries out periodic audits; Body may perform unexpected visits and tests. 5 Certificate of Conformity: Body issues CoC if supplier has effective certified safety system; Body records in SASO portal; supplier provides written Declaration of Conformity for 10 years after placement; Body informs regulatory authorities of issued/withdrawn approvals.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p020_c001", "title": "Annex (3) Conformity Assessment Form (Type 1a) – Type Approval. Type approval: N", "content": "Annex (3) Conformity Assessment Form (Type 1a) – Type Approval. Type approval: Notified Body reviews technical design and declares compliance. Two methods: A) examination of representative sample (production model); B) assessment by auditing technical documentation (design model) + examining sample of hazardous parts. 2/1 Submission: manufacturer submits request with name/address, written declaration, technical documentation including risk analysis, design/manufacturing drawings, description, list of standards, test reports, samples, supporting evidence.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p021_c001", "title": "2/2 Tasks of Notified Body: 2/2/1 Study technical documentation. 2/2/2 For sampl", "content": "2/2 Tasks of Notified Body: 2/2/1 Study technical documentation. 2/2/2 For samples: ensure manufacturing conforms to documentation; carry out appropriate tests; agree with manufacturer on test venue. 2/2/3 Decisions: issue assessment report; issue Type Approval Certificate if type meets requirements; if non-conforming, notify applicant with justifications; follow technological developments; manufacturer must inform Body of modifications that affect conformity; Bodies inform SASO of issued/withdrawn certificates; Bodies inform other accredited Bodies of rejected/suspended/restricted certificate", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc05_p024_c001", "title": "Annex (4) Supplier Declaration of Conformity Form. To be filled on company lette", "content": "Annex (4) Supplier Declaration of Conformity Form. To be filled on company letterhead. 1) Supplier data: name, address, contact person, email, tel, fax. 2) Product details: trademark, type, description, category, reference standards/technical specifications. Declaration: \"We acknowledge that the above-mentioned product conforms to the Saudi technical regulation ( ) and the Saudi standards included therein.\" Signature, company, date.", "source": "Leather-products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc06_p001_c001", "title": "List of Standards Relevant to the Implementation of the Technical Regulation for", "content": "List of Standards Relevant to the Implementation of the Technical Regulation for Autonomous Vehicles. (Table of standards in Arabic and English with standard numbers).", "source": "List-of-Standards-Relevant-to-the-Implementation-of-the-Technical-Regulation-for-Autonomous-Vehicles", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc06_p002_c001", "title": "SAE J3016 – Taxonomy and definitions for automated driving systems for on-road v", "content": "SAE J3016 – Taxonomy and definitions for automated driving systems for on-road vehicles. SASO ISO 26262-1 to -12 – Road vehicles – Functional safety (parts 1-12). IEEE 2846 – Minimum assumptions and expected scenarios for safety models in ADS. SAE J3187 – STPA (System-Theoretic Process Analysis) recommended practices. SASO ISO/PAS 21448 – Road vehicles – Safety of the intended functionality (SOTIF).", "source": "List-of-Standards-Relevant-to-the-Implementation-of-the-Technical-Regulation-for-Autonomous-Vehicles", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc06_p003_c001", "title": "SASO ISO 22737 – Low-speed automated driving systems (LSAD). ISO 19157 – Geograp", "content": "SASO ISO 22737 – Low-speed automated driving systems (LSAD). ISO 19157 – Geographic information – Data quality. ISO/TS 19158 – Quality assurance of data supply. ISO/IEC 2382-1 – IT vocabulary. ISO/IEC/IEEE 15288 – System life cycle processes. SASO IEC 61508-1 to -5 – Functional safety of electrical/electronic/programmable electronic safety-related systems. SASO ISO 34502 – Test scenarios for automated driving systems. EU 2022/1426 – Procedures for type-approval of ADS for fully automated vehicles. EU 2022/2236 – Technical requirements for vehicles (small series, software update). UN Regulation", "source": "List-of-Standards-Relevant-to-the-Implementation-of-the-Technical-Regulation-for-Autonomous-Vehicles", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc06_p004_c001", "title": "UN Regulation No 79 – Steering equipment. UN Regulation No 157 – Automated Lane ", "content": "UN Regulation No 79 – Steering equipment. UN Regulation No 157 – Automated Lane Keeping Systems (ALKS). UN Regulation No 158 – Reversing motion devices. UN Regulation No 160 – Event Data Recorder (EDR). SASO-ISO-8820-1/6 – Fuse-links. SASO GSO 41 – Front/rear exterior protection devices (bumpers). SASO GSO 42 – General requirements for motor vehicles. SASO 469 – Dimensions and weights. SASO GSO 279/280 – Car upholstery – testing methods and fabric. SASO 289 – Retro-reflective number plates. SASO GSO 290 – Instruction manual for appliances. SASO GSO 581 – Storage requirements for tires. SASO GS", "source": "List-of-Standards-Relevant-to-the-Implementation-of-the-Technical-Regulation-for-Autonomous-Vehicles", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc06_p005_c001", "title": "SASO GSO 1711 – Speed limiters Part 1. SASO GSO 1780 – Vehicle Identification Nu", "content": "SASO GSO 1711 – Speed limiters Part 1. SASO GSO 1780 – Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) requirements. SASO GSO 1781 – World Manufacturer Identifier. SASO GSO 1782 – VIN location and attachment. SASO GSO 1783 – Tire treadwear/traction/temperature grading. SASO GSO 1784 – Tire temperature resistance testing. SASO GSO ISO 3537 – Safety glazing – mechanical tests. SASO GSO ISO 3538 – Safety glasses – optical properties. SASO GSO ISO 6311 – Brake lining – internal shear strength. SASO GSO ISO 1585 – Engine test code – net power. SASO GSO ECE 13H – Braking system of passenger cars and multi-purpo", "source": "List-of-Standards-Relevant-to-the-Implementation-of-the-Technical-Regulation-for-Autonomous-Vehicles", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc06_p006_c001", "title": "SASO GSO ISO 3917 – Safety glazing – resistance to radiation/heat/humidity/fire.", "content": "SASO GSO ISO 3917 – Safety glazing – resistance to radiation/heat/humidity/fire. SASO GSO ISO 6310 – Brake linings – compressive strain test. SASO GSO ISO 6312 – Brake linings – shear test. SASO GSO ISO 6313 – Brake linings – effect of heat on dimensions. SASO GSO ISO 4000-2 – Passenger car tires and rims. ISO 23273 – Fuel cell road vehicles – hydrogen safety. ECE R 100 – Electric power train safety (including rechargeable battery systems). FMVSS 305 – Electric-powered vehicles. UN-R134 – Hydrogen fuel cell vehicles (HFCV) safety. UN-R12 – Steering mechanism protection in impact. UN-R10 – Elec", "source": "List-of-Standards-Relevant-to-the-Implementation-of-the-Technical-Regulation-for-Autonomous-Vehicles", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc06_p007_c001", "title": "SASO GSO ISO 4209-2 – Truck/bus tires and rims (metric series) – rims. SASO ISO ", "content": "SASO GSO ISO 4209-2 – Truck/bus tires and rims (metric series) – rims. SASO ISO 7141 – Light alloy wheels – impact test. SASO Hydrogen Technical Regulation – Safety of hydrogen fueled vehicles. SASO GSO ISO 3894 – Commercial vehicle wheels/rims – test methods. SASO IEC 60095-1/2 – Lead-acid starter batteries – requirements and dimensions. SASO GSO ISO 3006 – Passenger car wheels – test methods. UN Regulation No 34 – Fire risk prevention. FMVSS 301 – Fuel system integrity. SASO GSO 36 – Frontal impact test. SASO GSO 40 – Impact strength. GSO ECE 12 – Steering mechanism protection. UN Regulation", "source": "List-of-Standards-Relevant-to-the-Implementation-of-the-Technical-Regulation-for-Autonomous-Vehicles", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc06_p008_c001", "title": "GSO ECE 95 – Lateral collision occupant protection. FMVSS 214 – Side impact prot", "content": "GSO ECE 95 – Lateral collision occupant protection. FMVSS 214 – Side impact protection. SASO GSO 39 – Roof strength test. FMVSS 216a – Roof crush resistance. UN Regulation No 10 – Electromagnetic compatibility. SASO GSO 98 – Flammability of interior materials. SASO GSO 99 – Sound signaling devices. UN Regulation No 28 – Audible warning devices. SASO GSO 51/52/53 – Passenger car tires (nomenclature, general requirements, test methods). SASO 2857 – Tire rolling resistance and wet grip. SASO 2938 – AM/FM/DAB+ radio receivers. SASO 2944 – eCall emergency calls. SASO 2955 – Front underrun protectiv", "source": "List-of-Standards-Relevant-to-the-Implementation-of-the-Technical-Regulation-for-Autonomous-Vehicles", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc06_p009_c001", "title": "UN Regulation No 83 – Pollutant emissions according to engine fuel. SASO GSO 419", "content": "UN Regulation No 83 – Pollutant emissions according to engine fuel. SASO GSO 419 – Door locks and hinges test methods. SASO GSO 420 – Door locks and hinges. UN Regulation No 11 – Door latches and retention components. SASO GSO 421 – Rear-view mirrors test methods. SASO GSO 422 – Rear-view mirrors. UN Regulation No 46 – Indirect vision devices. UN Regulation No 39 – Speedometer and odometer equipment. SASO GSO 96 – Safety belts test methods. SASO GSO 97 – Safety belts. UN Regulation No 14 – Safety-belt anchorages, ISOFIX. UNECE Regulation 44 – Child Restraint System (from MY2026). UNECE Regulat", "source": "List-of-Standards-Relevant-to-the-Implementation-of-the-Technical-Regulation-for-Autonomous-Vehicles", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc07_p001_c001", "title": "ITC\'s NTM survey data. Methodology and potential for research and policy advisor", "content": "ITC\'s NTM survey data. Methodology and potential for research and policy advisory. Anders Aeroe, Director, Division of Market Development, ITC. 25 June 2012.", "source": "NTM.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc07_p002_c001", "title": "ITC\'s firm-level NTM survey. ITC currently collects survey data on Non-Tariff Me", "content": "ITC\'s firm-level NTM survey. ITC currently collects survey data on Non-Tariff Measures (NTMs) in more than 30 developing countries. Up to 1,500 firms participate in phone-screen, and up to 300 firms in face-to-face interviews. Objectives: Identify measures that exporting firms perceive as burdensome at product- and partner country-level. Provide unique firm-level dataset with comparable and consistent cross-country and cross-sector information.", "source": "NTM.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc07_p003_c001", "title": "Facts and figures on ITC\'s NTM survey data I. NTM survey data covers trade in go", "content": "Facts and figures on ITC\'s NTM survey data I. NTM survey data covers trade in goods. Currently 13 countries fully processed, 30 countries foreseen. At least 90% of total export value of each participating country. 13 sectors with at least 2% share in total exports (excl. arms and minerals). Each burdensome measure classified according to NTM classification (over 200 measures grouped into 16 categories).", "source": "NTM.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc07_p004_c001", "title": "Facts and figures on ITC\'s NTM survey data II. Two steps: 1) phone screens: addr", "content": "Facts and figures on ITC\'s NTM survey data II. Two steps: 1) phone screens: address, main export product, exporter status, structure (# employees, share female). 2) face-to-face interviews with companies that reported difficulties: turnover, export share, all trade products/partner countries, relevant government-imposed regulations, affected products (HS6), partner country, country applying regulation.", "source": "NTM.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc07_p005_c001", "title": "Analyses at different levels: Company level (NTM/PO yes/no, all firm characteris", "content": "Analyses at different levels: Company level (NTM/PO yes/no, all firm characteristics); Product-partner level (NTM/PO location, HS6, partner country, firm characteristics); \'Case\' level (detailed problem description, HS6, partner country, firm characteristics).", "source": "NTM.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc07_p006_c001", "title": "Overview of surveyed countries (table): Burkina Faso (442 phone, 103 facing NTMs", "content": "Overview of surveyed countries (table): Burkina Faso (442 phone, 103 facing NTMs, 69 face-to-face), Egypt (869, 328, 187), Jamaica (608, 210, 122), Kenya (764, 563, 286), Madagascar (393, 210, 158), Malawi (140, 93, 26), Mauritius (602, 169, 112), Morocco (794, 345, 256), Paraguay (406, 246, 97), Peru (960, 386, 119), Rwanda (354, 246, 140), Sri Lanka (521, 355, 107), Uruguay (458, 247, 95).", "source": "NTM.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc07_p007_c001", "title": "How do we currently use ITC\'s NTM survey data? Public-private dialogue. Country ", "content": "How do we currently use ITC\'s NTM survey data? Public-private dialogue. Country reports (Sri Lanka, Burkina Faso, Morocco, Peru, Uruguay, Paraguay, Egypt, Malawi, Kenya, Madagascar, Rwanda). Other publications: League of Arab States Regional Integration, Business Perspectives on Obstacles to Trade, etc.", "source": "NTM.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc07_p008_c001", "title": "What\'s next? Data currently for 18 countries; initiative foresees 30+ countries.", "content": "What\'s next? Data currently for 18 countries; initiative foresees 30+ countries. Extending coverage allows replication of sector/firm-specific effects within countries and obtaining new results across countries (which types of countries are mostly affected?).", "source": "NTM.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc08_p001_c001", "title": "GOVERNMENT & TRADE SERVICES. SASO SABER PCoC & SCoC.", "content": "GOVERNMENT & TRADE SERVICES. SASO SABER PCoC & SCoC.", "source": "SASO-PCoC---SCoC--SABER-Brochure.pdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc08_p002_c001", "title": "Applus+ at a glance: worldwide leader in TIC sector, 26,000+ employees in 68+ co", "content": "Applus+ at a glance: worldwide leader in TIC sector, 26,000+ employees in 68+ countries. Market leader in global TIC services. Energy & Industry Division: enhances performance and profitability, minimizes operational/environmental risks. Core services: inspection, non-destructive testing, engineering, supervision, testing, vendor surveillance, energy efficiency, Government & Trade Services.", "source": "SASO-PCoC---SCoC--SABER-Brochure.pdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc08_p003_c001", "title": "Applus+ GTS department appointed by SASO as approved conformity assessment body ", "content": "Applus+ GTS department appointed by SASO as approved conformity assessment body to issue PCoC and SCoC. Scope of accreditation covers Technical Regulations: Construction and Building Material (metal alloys, insulation, bricks/tiles/ceramic/sanitary ware, doors/windows); Mechanical (portable machines, mobile machinery, auto spare parts, motorcycle); Electrical (batteries, EMC, RoHS, low voltage); Textile (footwear, textile products, PPE, leather products); Chemical (food safety in kitchen tools).", "source": "SASO-PCoC---SCoC--SABER-Brochure.pdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc08_p005_c001", "title": "Certification Process: Step 1: Product Information Collection – determine tests,", "content": "Certification Process: Step 1: Product Information Collection – determine tests, sample collection to ISO/IEC 17025 accredited lab. Step 2: PCoC – review request via SABER portal, distributor submits documentation, evaluation, factory audit (Type 3 only), issuance via SABER. Step 3: SCoC – distributor requests SCoC through SABER, submits shipment documentation, issuance per shipment.", "source": "SASO-PCoC---SCoC--SABER-Brochure.pdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc09_p001_c001", "title": "1. Scope of Service: UL Solutions assesses products for compliance with SASO tec", "content": "1. Scope of Service: UL Solutions assesses products for compliance with SASO technical regulations. Upon compliance, issues SABER PCoC stating compliant standards/technical requirements. Studies and approves SABER SCoC requests for products covered by PCoC for Saudi customs clearance.", "source": "Saudi-Arabia-SABER-Program-Service-Terms-b.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc09_p001_c002", "title": "2. Information, Data, Materials: Client provides test data/reports from ISO/IEC ", "content": "2. Information, Data, Materials: Client provides test data/reports from ISO/IEC 17025 accredited lab (ILAC/APAC MRA), photographs, rating plates, labels, instruction manuals in Arabic/English. Declares authorization to use documents owned by original manufacturer.", "source": "Saudi-Arabia-SABER-Program-Service-Terms-b.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc09_p001_c003", "title": "3. Work Schedules and Cancellation: Schedules are estimates. Sole remedy for del", "content": "3. Work Schedules and Cancellation: Schedules are estimates. Sole remedy for delay is termination. Client may discontinue/postpone with written notice, pays for services performed before notice. UL not liable for errors/deficiencies; client shall not use UL name in connection with products.", "source": "Saudi-Arabia-SABER-Program-Service-Terms-b.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc09_p001_c004", "title": "4. Fees: Price established by Quotation. Price guideline set by SASO. Costs for ", "content": "4. Fees: Price established by Quotation. Price guideline set by SASO. Costs for testing/evaluation/inspection/certification quoted separately, subject to change with reasonable notice. 5. Compliance with Saudi Standards: Products must comply with SASO requirements, including audits to authorized factories. Client agrees to give authorized Saudi representative full factory access. Factory visits billed at current rates.", "source": "Saudi-Arabia-SABER-Program-Service-Terms-b.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc09_p002_c001", "title": "7. Responsibilities of Client: Client responsible for all products shipped under", "content": "7. Responsibilities of Client: Client responsible for all products shipped under SABER SCoC, including recall costs, indirect/direct damages, fines levied upon UL by SASO due to non-conforming products. Client agrees UL may notify SASO/Saudi Customs of non-conformity not corrected.", "source": "Saudi-Arabia-SABER-Program-Service-Terms-b.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc09_p002_c002", "title": "8. Responsibilities of Manufacturer/Supplier: Cooperate with Regulatory Bodies a", "content": "8. Responsibilities of Manufacturer/Supplier: Cooperate with Regulatory Bodies and Market Surveillance Authorities, providing technical documentation, test reports, and other documented information as requested by UL CAB. 9. Responsibilities of UL SASO approved CAB: SABER is SASO\'s system; UL not responsible for malfunctions or errors. Validity/expiration check is certificate holder\'s responsibility. UL not responsible for customs issues if models/quantities differ from SCoC.", "source": "Saudi-Arabia-SABER-Program-Service-Terms-b.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc10_p001_c001", "title": "UNDERSTANDING THE NEW CERTIFICATION CUSTOMS PLATFORM SABER. \"Saudi market offers", "content": "UNDERSTANDING THE NEW CERTIFICATION CUSTOMS PLATFORM SABER. \"Saudi market offers unlimited business opportunities...\" Larbi Elattari. INTRODUCTION/DEFINITION OF SABER: SASO implemented SALEEM and forced registration on SABER platform through seven timeline phases. Enforced Jan 1, 2019, SABER replaces old CoC system. SABER implemented gradually to streamline product registration, conformity assessment, and shipment.", "source": "s-ge20184-c7-saudi-arabien-saber.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc10_p001_c002", "title": "REGULATED/AFFECTED PRODUCTS: Regulated products (high/medium risk) require SCoC ", "content": "REGULATED/AFFECTED PRODUCTS: Regulated products (high/medium risk) require SCoC that necessitates prior PCoC. Non-regulated products (low risk) need self-Declaration of Conformity (sDoC) issued through SABER.", "source": "s-ge20184-c7-saudi-arabien-saber.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc10_p002_c001", "title": "THE CONCERNED REGULATIONS AND IMPLEMENTED DATES: Jan 2019 – Gas Appliances and A", "content": "THE CONCERNED REGULATIONS AND IMPLEMENTED DATES: Jan 2019 – Gas Appliances and Accessories (M.A.-156-16-04-04). Apr 2019 – Children Toys (BD-131704-01), Low Voltage Electrical Equipment (BD-142004-01), Lubricating Oils (S.V.-155-16-03-01). Jun 2019 – Lifts (M.A. 161-17-07-05), Building Materials Part 1-4 (Metals/Alloys, Insulation, Hydraulic Connections, Bricks/Tiles/Ceramic), Paints (M.A.-155.16.03.03), Electric Scooters (M.A.-155-06-03-04), Degradable Plastic Products (M.A.-156-16-04-03), Electrical Batteries (M.A.-166-18-04-02).", "source": "s-ge20184-c7-saudi-arabien-saber.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc10_p002_c002", "title": "Nov 2019 – Auto Spare Parts (B.D.-162-17-04-02), Personal Protective Equipment a", "content": "Nov 2019 – Auto Spare Parts (B.D.-162-17-04-02), Personal Protective Equipment and Clothing (M.A.-165-18-04-04). Dec 2019 – Small-Solar Photovoltaic Systems (M.A. 165-18-04-03), Textile Products (M.A.-164-18-05-02), Trailers and Semi-Trailers (M.A.-162-17-07-04), Detergents (M.A. 155-16-03-02).", "source": "s-ge20184-c7-saudi-arabien-saber.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc10_p003_c001", "title": "Jan 2020 – Photovoltaic Cells (M.A. 165-18-04-03), Front/Rear/Side Barriers for ", "content": "Jan 2020 – Photovoltaic Cells (M.A. 165-18-04-03), Front/Rear/Side Barriers for Trucks (M.A.-161-17-07-04). TBD: Games and Amusement Parks, Adhesives, Ornaments/Decorations, Building Materials Part 5 (Pipes), Telecommunications Devices, Packaging, Food Contact Materials, Shoes and Leather, Simple Pressure Devices, Fire Fighting Equipment, Fireworks, Electric Vehicles, Doors/Windows, Papers, Machinery Safety Part 1, Tyres (Gulf TR), Electronic Smoking Devices, Motorcycle, Tanks Part 1 (Petroleum Transport), Energy Efficiency, Water Rationalization Tools, SASO IECEE Recognition, Modified Vehicle", "source": "s-ge20184-c7-saudi-arabien-saber.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc10_p004_c001", "title": "SABER CERTIFICATION PROCESS (Regulated Products) – Two stages: Stage 1: PCoC. Va", "content": "SABER CERTIFICATION PROCESS (Regulated Products) – Two stages: Stage 1: PCoC. Valid for 1 year. Steps: Importer requests PCoC, enters product details (HS code), selects CB, pays fees, CB contacts exporter for documents, CB submits approved documents to SABER, PCoC issued. Required docs: test reports, quality certificates, risk assessment, design/dimensions/plans/photos.", "source": "s-ge20184-c7-saudi-arabien-saber.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc10_p004_c002", "title": "Stage 2: SCoC. For each shipment, verifies valid PCoC exists. Steps: Importer re", "content": "Stage 2: SCoC. For each shipment, verifies valid PCoC exists. Steps: Importer requests SCoC, pays fees, CB verifies PCoC, SCoC issued. Required: PCoC + shipment documents (invoice, packing list, bill of lading).", "source": "s-ge20184-c7-saudi-arabien-saber.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc10_p005_c001", "title": "FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS: What is SABER? Electronic platform for conformity as", "content": "FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS: What is SABER? Electronic platform for conformity assessment certificates before entering Saudi market. What products must be registered? All products regulated by SASO. Who must register? Importers/manufacturers with Saudi commercial register. Fees to open account? No. Communication officer? Employee appointed by company to access system. Other authorities providing CoC? Yes, SASO-accepted CBs list on SABER.", "source": "s-ge20184-c7-saudi-arabien-saber.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc10_p006_c001", "title": "FAQs continued: Can CBs outside Saudi issue CoC? Yes, if accredited by SASO. Is ", "content": "FAQs continued: Can CBs outside Saudi issue CoC? Yes, if accredited by SASO. Is SABER the only platform? Yes. What documents required? Depends on product and technical regulation. What if no CoC? Products prevented from entry, fined. Fees? 500 SAR per certificate, non-refundable. Can same certificate be used for same product made in different country? No. How to handle tens of thousands of spare parts? Account managers will assist. How does SABER affect manufacturers? Registration responsibility shifts to Saudi importer.", "source": "s-ge20184-c7-saudi-arabien-saber.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc10_p007_c001", "title": "TAKEAWAYS: SABER becomes only system for clearing goods through Saudi customs. B", "content": "TAKEAWAYS: SABER becomes only system for clearing goods through Saudi customs. Both PCoC and SCoC mandatory. Shipment Certificate required for each consignment. Certification can be obtained online by Saudi-based importer. Contact: Larbi Elattari, Swiss Business Hub Middle East.", "source": "s-ge20184-c7-saudi-arabien-saber.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc11_p001_c001", "title": "الدليل الإرشادي للائحة الفنية للمنتجات النسيجية - الإصدار الثاني ١٠ ديسمبر ٢٠٢٤.", "content": "الدليل الإرشادي للائحة الفنية للمنتجات النسيجية - الإصدار الثاني ١٠ ديسمبر ٢٠٢٤. Saudi Standards.", "source": "Technical-Regulation-Guide-for-Textile-Products-Second-Edition.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc11_p004_c001", "title": "تمهيد: اعتمد مجلس إدارة الهيئة السعودية للمواصفات والمقاييس والجودة اللائحة الفن", "content": "تمهيد: اعتمد مجلس إدارة الهيئة السعودية للمواصفات والمقاييس والجودة اللائحة الفنية للمنتجات النسيجية – الإصدار الثاني كإحدى اللوائح الفنية المستهدفة ضمن خطة البرنامج السعودي لسلامة المنتجات، الذي يهدف إلى حماية صحة وسلامة المستهلك والمحافظة على البيئة وذلك بالتأكد من مدى مطابقة المنتجات المعروضة في الأسواق لمتطلبات اللوائح الفنية وما تشمله من مواصفات قياسية. تحدد اللوائح الفنية إجراءات تقويم المطابقة للمنتجات المشمولة بمجال اللائحة بما يضمن استيفاء جهات تقويم المطابقة المقبولة لمتطلبات اللائحة الفنية والإدارية بالإضافة إلى دور الجهات الرقابية بإلزام الموردين والصناعيين المحليين بتطبيق هذه اللو", "source": "Technical-Regulation-Guide-for-Textile-Products-Second-Edition.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc11_p004_c002", "title": "الخط الزمني: اعتمدت اللائحة الفنية للمنتجات النسيجية في مجلس الإدارة رقم 164 بتا", "content": "الخط الزمني: اعتمدت اللائحة الفنية للمنتجات النسيجية في مجلس الإدارة رقم 164 بتاريخ 1439/07/19 هـ (2018/04/05). اعتمدت تحديث اللائحة في مجلس الإدارة رقم 195 بتاريخ 1445/06/15 هـ (2023/12/28). نشرت اللائحة في الجريدة الرسمية (أم القرى) بتاريخ 1445/06/30 هـ (2024/01/12). دخلت اللائحة حيز التنفيذ في المنافذ والمصانع بتاريخ 1446/01/03 هـ (2024/07/10). دخلت اللائحة حيز التنفيذ في الأسواق بتاريخ 1446/07/11 هـ (2025/01/11).", "source": "Technical-Regulation-Guide-for-Textile-Products-Second-Edition.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc11_p005_c001", "title": "المصطلحات والتعاريف: اللائحة الفنية – وثيقة معتمدة من مجلس الإدارة تضع خصائص الم", "content": "المصطلحات والتعاريف: اللائحة الفنية – وثيقة معتمدة من مجلس الإدارة تضع خصائص المنتجات والعمليات المرتبطة بها وطرائق إنتاجها. المواصفة القياسية – وثيقة تحدد صفات السلعة أو المادة أو الخدمة. عالمة الجودة السعودية – عالمة اعتمدتها الهيئة تدل على أن المنشأة ذات نظام إدارة جودة. المنتَج – المنتجات النسيجية المشمولة باللائحة. المنتجات النسيجية – كل منتج بأي صيغته الخام أو المصنَّعة أو نصف المصنَّعة التي تتألف حصرياً من ألياف النسيج. الألياف النسيجية – وحدة مكوِّنة للمادة الخام في الصناعة النسيجية. البطانة – عنصر يستخدم في صناعة المالبس. الألياف غير المعروفة – مادة غير مدرجة وليست مقدرة في بطاقة البي", "source": "Technical-Regulation-Guide-for-Textile-Products-Second-Edition.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc11_p006_c001", "title": "مجال اللائحة الفنية للمنتجات النسيجية: تشمل جميع منتجات الغزل والنسيج التي تطرح ", "content": "مجال اللائحة الفنية للمنتجات النسيجية: تشمل جميع منتجات الغزل والنسيج التي تطرح في أسواق المملكة: 1) كل المنتجات التي تتكون مما لا يقل عن 80% وزناً من ألياف النسيج (ألياف وغزول وخيوط وستائر ومفروشات وسجاد ومالبس وأقمشة ومنسوجات تقنية). 2) كل الأثاث المستخدم كأغطية ومظلات وواقيات الشمس التي تتكون مما لا يقل عن 80% وزناً من ألياف النسيج، وتشمل: أ) الطبقة العليا من الأرضيات متعددة الطبقات. ب) أغطية المفارش والأفرشة. ج) أغطية الأجهزة والمنتجات الخاصة بالتخييم، شريطة أن تكون المكونات نسيجية وتشكل 80% على الأقل من طبقات الأغطية العلوية. د) كل منسوج يشكل جزءاً لا يتجزأ من منتج آخر (الحقائب وأغطية الر", "source": "Technical-Regulation-Guide-for-Textile-Products-Second-Edition.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc11_p007_c001", "title": "أمثلة لبعض المنتجات المشمولة بمجال اللائحة. يجب على المورد المسؤول عن وضع مالبس ", "content": "أمثلة لبعض المنتجات المشمولة بمجال اللائحة. يجب على المورد المسؤول عن وضع مالبس الأطفال والمنتجات الملامسة للجلد بشكل مباشر الحصول على شهادة مطابقة (TYPE 3): مالبس أطفال، مالبس داخلية، الأحرام (الحفائظ)، حفائظ أطفال، الفوط الصحية للنساء، مالبس سباحة.", "source": "Technical-Regulation-Guide-for-Textile-Products-Second-Edition.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc11_p008_c001", "title": "يجب على المورد المسؤول عن وضع بقية المنتجات الخاضعة لهذه اللائحة الحصول على شهاد", "content": "يجب على المورد المسؤول عن وضع بقية المنتجات الخاضعة لهذه اللائحة الحصول على شهادة مطابقة (TYPE 1A): جوارب، خيمة الرحلات، مالبس الزي الموحد، منشفة، الطبقة العليا من الأرضيات متعددة الطبقات، أغطية المفارش والفرش، أغطية الأجهزة والمنتجات الخاصة بالتخييم، خيوط ونسج الحرير والصوف والقطن، ألياف نسيجية نباتية أخرى، ألياف تركيبية أو اصطناعية غير مستمرة، سجاد وأغطية أرضيات، شعيرات تركيبية أو اصطناعية، ألياف نسيجية للحشو، نسج مشربة أو مطلية أو مغطاة، ألبسة وتوابع ألبسة من غير المصنرات أو الكروشيه، الزي المدرسي، الكمامات القماشية.", "source": "Technical-Regulation-Guide-for-Textile-Products-Second-Edition.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc11_p011_c001", "title": "الاستثناءات التي جاءت بها اللائحة الفنية للمنتجات النسيجية: يستثنى من تطبيق هذه ", "content": "الاستثناءات التي جاءت بها اللائحة الفنية للمنتجات النسيجية: يستثنى من تطبيق هذه اللائحة: المنتجات التي صممت للأغراض الطبية أو الإدعاء الطبي (تندرج تحت متطلبات ولوائح الهيئة العامة للغذاء والدواء). الأحذية الخاضعة للائحة الفنية للأحذية وملحقاتها.", "source": "Technical-Regulation-Guide-for-Textile-Products-Second-Edition.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc11_p012_c001", "title": "متطلبات اللائحة: استيفاء متطلبات اللائحة والمواصفات القياسية يعد شرطاً أساسياً ق", "content": "متطلبات اللائحة: استيفاء متطلبات اللائحة والمواصفات القياسية يعد شرطاً أساسياً قبل عرض المنتجات النسيجية في أسواق المملكة. من أهم المتطلبات: وجود بطاقة البيانات الإيضاحية، تقارير اختبارات المواد الضارة وفقاً للمواصفات ذات العلاقة من مختبر معتمد، ملف فني يثبت استيفاء جميع المتطلبات للحصول على شهادة المطابقة. المتطلبات المترولوجية: استخدام وحدات النظام الدولي (SI units) أو مضاعفاتها أو أجزائها أثناء التصميم أو التصنيع أو التداول.", "source": "Technical-Regulation-Guide-for-Textile-Products-Second-Edition.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc11_p014_c001", "title": "أهم الاختبارات: يجب إجراء الاختبارات المحددة في اللائحة للمواصفات القياسية المذك", "content": "أهم الاختبارات: يجب إجراء الاختبارات المحددة في اللائحة للمواصفات القياسية المذكورة في الملحق رقم (1). ومن أهمها: الرقم الهيدروجيني (pH) – يجب أن تكون قيم درجة الحموضة المسموح بها ضمن الحدود الآمنة للاستخدام. ثبات اللون – للغسيل والعرق والاحتكاك. ثبات اللعاب – لمالبس الأطفال. المواد الكيميائية الخطرة – CMR (مسرطنة، مطفرة، سامة للتكاثر)، PBT/vPvB (ثابتة، متراكمة، سامة)، مواد كيميائية لها آثار خطيرة دائمة على البشر أو البيئة. المواد الكيميائية الضارة – الفورمالديهايد، المعادن الثقيلة، الفينولات، الأصباغ، الأمينات المسرطنة، مثبطات اللهب، بقايا المبيدات، الفثالات، المركبات الكلورية العضوية، مركبات", "source": "Technical-Regulation-Guide-for-Textile-Products-Second-Edition.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc11_p016_c001", "title": "التسجيل في منصة سابر: يجب التسجيل بصفة \'مستخدم جديد\' وتعبئة البيانات المطلوبة في", "content": "التسجيل في منصة سابر: يجب التسجيل بصفة \'مستخدم جديد\' وتعبئة البيانات المطلوبة في الصفحة الرئيسية لمنصة سابر الإلكترونية. تفعيل حساب المستفيد من خلال البريد الإلكتروني. تسجيل المنتجات من خلال البحث بالرمز الجمركي أو اسم المنتج للحصول على شهادة المطابقة.", "source": "Technical-Regulation-Guide-for-Textile-Products-Second-Edition.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc11_p020_c001", "title": "شهادة الإرسالية (SCoC): بعد حصول المنتجات على شهادة المطابقة وتسجيلها في منصة سا", "content": "شهادة الإرسالية (SCoC): بعد حصول المنتجات على شهادة المطابقة وتسجيلها في منصة سابر، تُسجَّل شهادة الإرسالية لكل شحنة قبل شحنها وعرضها في الأسواق، وذلك باختيار المنتجات المراد استيرادها وإكمال البيانات المطلوبة: بيانات الفاتورة (تاريخ الفاتورة، رقم الفاتورة، قيمة إجمالي الفاتورة، العملة، اسم المورد وعنوانه). بيانات المنتجات وتحديد الموديلات والكميات ودولة الشحن. يرسل الطلب لجهة تقويم المطابقة للتأكد من صحة البيانات. تُصدر شهادة الإرسالية. نموذج الشهادة يتضمن إقراراً بأن جميع بيانات المنتجات صحيحة ومطابقة للمواصفات القياسية السعودية واللوائح الفنية ذات العلاقة.", "source": "Technical-Regulation-Guide-for-Textile-Products-Second-Edition.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p001_c001", "title": "Saudi Standards, Metrology and Quality Organization SASO. Technical Regulation f", "content": "Saudi Standards, Metrology and Quality Organization SASO. Technical Regulation for Footwear and their Accessories. Approved in SASO Board of Directors meeting No. (177) on 28/02/1442 AH (15/10/2020). Published in Official Gazette on 12/04/1442 AH (27/11/2020 AD). Version (1). Note: Only Arabic version is authentic.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p002_c001", "title": "Contents: Article (1) Terms and Definitions; (2) Scope; (3) Objectives; (4) Supp", "content": "Contents: Article (1) Terms and Definitions; (2) Scope; (3) Objectives; (4) Supplier\'s Obligations; (5) Labelling; (6) Conformity Assessment Procedures; (7) Responsibilities of Regulatory Authorities; (8) Market Surveillance Authorities; (9) Violations and Penalties; (10) General Provisions; (11) Transitional Provisions; (12) Publication; plus Annexes 1A, 1B, 2, 3, 4.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p003_c001", "title": "Preamble: Based on WTO accession, Council of Ministers Decree No. 244, and SASO ", "content": "Preamble: Based on WTO accession, Council of Ministers Decree No. 244, and SASO Statute Articles 3, 4, 6, SASO developed this Technical Regulation. The regulation includes essential requirements and conformity assessment procedures.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p004_c001", "title": "Article (1) Terms and Definitions: KSA, Board, SASO, Regulatory Authorities, Mar", "content": "Article (1) Terms and Definitions: KSA, Board, SASO, Regulatory Authorities, Market Surveillance Authorities, Technical Regulation, Standard, Essential Requirements, Market Surveillance, Hazard(s), Risk(s), Supplier (manufacturer resident in KSA or agent/importer), Conformity Assessment Procedures, Notified Bodies, Certificate of Conformity, Supplier Declaration of Conformity, Saudi Quality Mark, Placing on Market, Making Available on Market, Withdrawal, Recall, Product (footwear excluding socks), Footwear, Insole, Outsole, Safety (Protective) Footwear, Professional Footwear, Label.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p006_c001", "title": "Article (2) Scope: 2/1 Applies to all types of footwear (leather, textile, plast", "content": "Article (2) Scope: 2/1 Applies to all types of footwear (leather, textile, plastic, or mixture). 2/2 Excluding medical footwear (under SFDA) and footwear classified as toys. 2/3 Professional footwear has additional requirements under PPE Technical Regulation. 2/4 Annex shows examples with HS codes. 2/5 Prohibited to place footwear made from skins of animals forbidden by law.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p006_c002", "title": "Article (3) Objectives: Lay out essential requirements, identify conformity asse", "content": "Article (3) Objectives: Lay out essential requirements, identify conformity assessment procedures to ensure product conformity for environment, health, consumer safety, and facilitate market surveillance.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p007_c001", "title": "Article (4) Supplier\'s Obligations: 4/1 General: Product must meet requirements ", "content": "Article (4) Supplier\'s Obligations: 4/1 General: Product must meet requirements in Annex standards; each footwear must have data label with information and size. 4/2 Technical: Meet technical requirements in Annex. 4/3 Metrological: Use SI units; footwear sizes per relevant standard. 4/4 Packaging: Packed in single carton, in pairs; packaging materials free of lead/heavy metals/harmful substances; recycling symbol on recyclable plastic bags.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p007_c002", "title": "Article (5) Labelling: Conditions: 5/1 Brand name and country of origin. 5/2 Dat", "content": "Article (5) Labelling: Conditions: 5/1 Brand name and country of origin. 5/2 Data in Arabic or Arabic+English. 5/3 Label affixed to each footwear, difficult to remove. 5/4 Meet technical requirements. 5/5 Information correct and proven. 5/6 Images/phrases not violate Islamic values. 5/7 Include required data.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p008_c001", "title": "Article (6) Conformity Assessment Procedures: 6/1 Only requirements of this regu", "content": "Article (6) Conformity Assessment Procedures: 6/1 Only requirements of this regulation. 6/2 Supplier must obtain CoC from notified body: Type 3 for infant footwear (under 36 months) – Annex 2; Type 1a for other products – Annex 3. 6/3 Notified body performs assessment. 6/4 Technical file includes: Supplier Declaration of Conformity (Annex 4), risk assessment, country of origin, test reports, list of standards, product explanatory booklet. Supplier must cooperate with authorities. 6/5 Products with Saudi Quality Mark deemed compliant.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p009_c001", "title": "Article (7) Responsibilities of Regulatory Authorities: Verify products fulfill ", "content": "Article (7) Responsibilities of Regulatory Authorities: Verify products fulfill conformity assessment procedures and technical documents; randomly sample and refer to labs; charge suppliers testing costs; withdraw non-conforming products and take legal actions.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p009_c002", "title": "Article (8) Market Surveillance Authorities: Enforce market surveillance on prod", "content": "Article (8) Market Surveillance Authorities: Enforce market surveillance on products in markets/warehouses; take samples; in case of non-conformity take administrative actions including withdrawal and recall. Article (9) Violations and Penalties: Prohibited to manufacture/import/launch/advertise non-conforming products. Non-conformity includes improper fixing of labels/marks, failure to issue CoC, incomplete technical documentation. Actions: withdrawal, destruction, export, recall. Penalties per Anti-Commercial Fraud Law.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p011_c001", "title": "Article (10) General Provisions: Supplier bears full legal responsibility. Must ", "content": "Article (10) General Provisions: Supplier bears full legal responsibility. Must comply with other applicable regulations (environment, security, safety, and Textile Products TR). Provide inspectors with information. Disputes referred to SASO committee. Supplier may resubmit after corrections. SASO may cancel CoC/Q-Mark. Modifications during validity annul certificate. SASO exclusively interprets. Article (11) Transitional Provisions: Supplier has 6 months from publication to take corrective actions. Non-complying products may be traded for up to one year. Article (12) Publication in Official G", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p013_c001", "title": "Annex (1-A) List of Standards: SASO-2931 (informal slippers), SASO ISO 19952 (vo", "content": "Annex (1-A) List of Standards: SASO-2931 (informal slippers), SASO ISO 19952 (vocabulary), ISO/TR 16178 (critical substances), SASO-2890 (women\'s footwear), SASO-1621 (terms and definitions), GSO 1956/2009 (harmful substances in textiles), SASO 1173 (identification labels), SASO 2889 (men\'s footwear), SASO 2891 (leisure footwear), SASO 2930 (sport footwear), SASO 2901 (children\'s footwear), ISO 9407 (Mondopoint sizing), ISO/TS 19407 (conversion), ISO/TS 19408 (vocabulary).", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p014_c001", "title": "Annex (1-B) List of Products and Customs Coding: 6401 (waterproof footwear), 640", "content": "Annex (1-B) List of Products and Customs Coding: 6401 (waterproof footwear), 6402 (other rubber/plastic), 6403 (leather uppers), 6404 (textile uppers), 6405 (other footwear), 6406 (parts), 681291000003 (footwear), 950670000003 (skates with wheels). Note: Saber platform has updated/approved codes.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p014_c002", "title": "Examples of footwear covered: indoor/outdoor slippers, high-leg footwear, sandal", "content": "Examples of footwear covered: indoor/outdoor slippers, high-leg footwear, sandals, canvas footwear, sports footwear, ski footwear, wrestling/boxing/cycling footwear, dance footwear, professional covers, single-use footwear.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p001_c001__2", "title": "Saudi Standards, Metrology and Quality Organization SASO. Technical Regulation f", "content": "Saudi Standards, Metrology and Quality Organization SASO. Technical Regulation for Footwear and their Accessories. Approved in SASO Board of Directors meeting No. (177) on 28/02/1442 AH (15/10/2020). Published in Official Gazette on 12/04/1442 AH (27/11/2020 AD). Version (1). Note: Only Arabic version is authentic.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p002_c001__2", "title": "Contents: Article (1) Terms and Definitions; (2) Scope; (3) Objectives; (4) Supp", "content": "Contents: Article (1) Terms and Definitions; (2) Scope; (3) Objectives; (4) Supplier\'s Obligations; (5) Labelling; (6) Conformity Assessment Procedures; (7) Responsibilities of Regulatory Authorities; (8) Market Surveillance Authorities; (9) Violations and Penalties; (10) General Provisions; (11) Transitional Provisions; (12) Publication; plus Annexes 1A, 1B, 2, 3, 4.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p003_c001__2", "title": "Preamble: Based on WTO accession, Council of Ministers Decree No. 244, and SASO ", "content": "Preamble: Based on WTO accession, Council of Ministers Decree No. 244, and SASO Statute Articles 3, 4, 6, SASO developed this Technical Regulation. The regulation includes essential requirements and conformity assessment procedures.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p004_c001__2", "title": "Article (1) Terms and Definitions: KSA, Board, SASO, Regulatory Authorities, Mar", "content": "Article (1) Terms and Definitions: KSA, Board, SASO, Regulatory Authorities, Market Surveillance Authorities, Technical Regulation, Standard, Essential Requirements, Market Surveillance, Hazard(s), Risk(s), Supplier (manufacturer resident in KSA or agent/importer), Conformity Assessment Procedures, Notified Bodies, Certificate of Conformity, Supplier Declaration of Conformity, Saudi Quality Mark, Placing on Market, Making Available on Market, Withdrawal, Recall, Product (footwear excluding socks), Footwear, Insole, Outsole, Safety (Protective) Footwear, Professional Footwear, Label.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p006_c001__2", "title": "Article (2) Scope: 2/1 Applies to all types of footwear (leather, textile, plast", "content": "Article (2) Scope: 2/1 Applies to all types of footwear (leather, textile, plastic, or mixture). 2/2 Excluding medical footwear (under SFDA) and footwear classified as toys. 2/3 Professional footwear has additional requirements under PPE Technical Regulation. 2/4 Annex shows examples with HS codes. 2/5 Prohibited to place footwear made from skins of animals forbidden by law.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p006_c002__2", "title": "Article (3) Objectives: Lay out essential requirements, identify conformity asse", "content": "Article (3) Objectives: Lay out essential requirements, identify conformity assessment procedures to ensure product conformity for environment, health, consumer safety, and facilitate market surveillance.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p007_c001__2", "title": "Article (4) Supplier\'s Obligations: 4/1 General: Product must meet requirements ", "content": "Article (4) Supplier\'s Obligations: 4/1 General: Product must meet requirements in Annex standards; each footwear must have data label with information and size. 4/2 Technical: Meet technical requirements in Annex. 4/3 Metrological: Use SI units; footwear sizes per relevant standard. 4/4 Packaging: Packed in single carton, in pairs; packaging materials free of lead/heavy metals/harmful substances; recycling symbol on recyclable plastic bags.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p007_c002__2", "title": "Article (5) Labelling: Conditions: 5/1 Brand name and country of origin. 5/2 Dat", "content": "Article (5) Labelling: Conditions: 5/1 Brand name and country of origin. 5/2 Data in Arabic or Arabic+English. 5/3 Label affixed to each footwear, difficult to remove. 5/4 Meet technical requirements. 5/5 Information correct and proven. 5/6 Images/phrases not violate Islamic values. 5/7 Include required data.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p008_c001__2", "title": "Article (6) Conformity Assessment Procedures: 6/1 Only requirements of this regu", "content": "Article (6) Conformity Assessment Procedures: 6/1 Only requirements of this regulation. 6/2 Supplier must obtain CoC from notified body: Type 3 for infant footwear (under 36 months) – Annex 2; Type 1a for other products – Annex 3. 6/3 Notified body performs assessment. 6/4 Technical file includes: Supplier Declaration of Conformity (Annex 4), risk assessment, country of origin, test reports, list of standards, product explanatory booklet. Supplier must cooperate with authorities. 6/5 Products with Saudi Quality Mark deemed compliant.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p009_c001__2", "title": "Article (7) Responsibilities of Regulatory Authorities: Verify products fulfill ", "content": "Article (7) Responsibilities of Regulatory Authorities: Verify products fulfill conformity assessment procedures and technical documents; randomly sample and refer to labs; charge suppliers testing costs; withdraw non-conforming products and take legal actions.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p009_c002__2", "title": "Article (8) Market Surveillance Authorities: Enforce market surveillance on prod", "content": "Article (8) Market Surveillance Authorities: Enforce market surveillance on products in markets/warehouses; take samples; in case of non-conformity take administrative actions including withdrawal and recall. Article (9) Violations and Penalties: Prohibited to manufacture/import/launch/advertise non-conforming products. Non-conformity includes improper fixing of labels/marks, failure to issue CoC, incomplete technical documentation. Actions: withdrawal, destruction, export, recall. Penalties per Anti-Commercial Fraud Law.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p011_c001__2", "title": "Article (10) General Provisions: Supplier bears full legal responsibility. Must ", "content": "Article (10) General Provisions: Supplier bears full legal responsibility. Must comply with other applicable regulations (environment, security, safety, and Textile Products TR). Provide inspectors with information. Disputes referred to SASO committee. Supplier may resubmit after corrections. SASO may cancel CoC/Q-Mark. Modifications during validity annul certificate. SASO exclusively interprets. Article (11) Transitional Provisions: Supplier has 6 months from publication to take corrective actions. Non-complying products may be traded for up to one year. Article (12) Publication in Official G", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p013_c001__2", "title": "Annex (1-A) List of Standards: SASO-2931 (informal slippers), SASO ISO 19952 (vo", "content": "Annex (1-A) List of Standards: SASO-2931 (informal slippers), SASO ISO 19952 (vocabulary), ISO/TR 16178 (critical substances), SASO-2890 (women\'s footwear), SASO-1621 (terms and definitions), GSO 1956/2009 (harmful substances in textiles), SASO 1173 (identification labels), SASO 2889 (men\'s footwear), SASO 2891 (leisure footwear), SASO 2930 (sport footwear), SASO 2901 (children\'s footwear), ISO 9407 (Mondopoint sizing), ISO/TS 19407 (conversion), ISO/TS 19408 (vocabulary).", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p014_c001__2", "title": "Annex (1-B) List of Products and Customs Coding: 6401 (waterproof footwear), 640", "content": "Annex (1-B) List of Products and Customs Coding: 6401 (waterproof footwear), 6402 (other rubber/plastic), 6403 (leather uppers), 6404 (textile uppers), 6405 (other footwear), 6406 (parts), 681291000003 (footwear), 950670000003 (skates with wheels). Note: Saber platform has updated/approved codes.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc12_p014_c002__2", "title": "Examples of footwear covered: indoor/outdoor slippers, high-leg footwear, sandal", "content": "Examples of footwear covered: indoor/outdoor slippers, high-leg footwear, sandals, canvas footwear, sports footwear, ski footwear, wrestling/boxing/cycling footwear, dance footwear, professional covers, single-use footwear.", "source": "TR-Footwear-and-their-Accessories.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc14_p001_c001", "title": "SASO Technical Regulation for Textile Products – Second Edition. Approved in Boa", "content": "SASO Technical Regulation for Textile Products – Second Edition. Approved in Board of Directors meeting No. (195) on 15/06/1445 AH (28/12/2023). Published in Official Gazette on 30/06/1445 AH (12/01/2024).", "source": "TR-Textile-Products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc14_p003_c001", "title": "تمهيد: بناءً على انضمام المملكة إلى منظمة التجارة العالمية، واتفاقية العوائق الف", "content": "تمهيد: بناءً على انضمام المملكة إلى منظمة التجارة العالمية، واتفاقية العوائق الفنية للتجارة (TBT)، والمادة الثالثة والرابعة والسادسة من تنظيم الهيئة، أعدت الهيئة هذه اللائحة الفنية. الملاحظة: هذا التمهيد وجميع ملاحق اللائحة جزء لا يتجزأ منها.", "source": "TR-Textile-Products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc14_p004_c001", "title": "المادة (1) المصطلحات والتعاريف: المملكة، المجلس، الهيئة، الجهات الرقابية، سلطات ", "content": "المادة (1) المصطلحات والتعاريف: المملكة، المجلس، الهيئة، الجهات الرقابية، سلطات مسح السوق، اللائحة الفنية، المواصفة القياسية، المتطلبات الأساسية، الخطر (Hazard)، الخطر (Risk)، مسح السوق، المورد (صانع المنتج في المملكة أو وكيله أو المستورد).", "source": "TR-Textile-Products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc14_p006_c001", "title": "المادة (2) المجال: 1/2 كل المنتجات التي تتكون مما لا يقل عن 80% وزناً من ألياف ا", "content": "المادة (2) المجال: 1/2 كل المنتجات التي تتكون مما لا يقل عن 80% وزناً من ألياف النسيج (ألياف وغزول وخيوط وستائر ومفروشات وسجاد ومالبس وأقمشة ومنسوجات تقنية). 2/2 كل الأثاث المستخدم كأغطية ومظلات وواقيات الشمس التي تتكون مما لا يقل عن 80% وزناً من ألياف النسيج، وتشمل الأجزاء المنسوجة في: أ) الطبقة العليا من الأرضيات متعددة الطبقات. ب) أغطية المفارش والأفرشة. ج) أغطية الأجهزة ومنتجات التخييم (شرط أن تشكل 80% من طبقات الأغطية العلوية). د) كل منسوج يشكل جزءاً لا يتجزأ من منتج آخر (الحقائب وأغطية الرأس). يستثنى من التطبيق: المنتجات الطبية (الهيئة العامة للغذاء والدواء)، والأحذية (اللائحة الفنية للأ", "source": "TR-Textile-Products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc14_p006_c002", "title": "المادة (3) الأهداف: تحديد المتطلبات الأساسية وإجراءات تقويم المطابقة للمنتجات ال", "content": "المادة (3) الأهداف: تحديد المتطلبات الأساسية وإجراءات تقويم المطابقة للمنتجات النسيجية لضمان مطابقتها والحفاظ على البيئة وصحة وسلامة المستهلك.", "source": "TR-Textile-Products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc14_p007_c001", "title": "المادة (4) متطلبات بطاقة البيانات الإيضاحية: يجب تعبئة بطاقة البيانات وفقاً للمو", "content": "المادة (4) متطلبات بطاقة البيانات الإيضاحية: يجب تعبئة بطاقة البيانات وفقاً للمواصفات القياسية في الملحق (1)، باستثناء المنتجات في الملحق (5). البيانات غير مضللة. تكون البطاقة مخيطة أو مثبتة بإحكام في الأماكن المتعارف عليها. تُستخدم أسماء الألياف الواردة في الملحق (2) حصرياً. لا توصف المنتجات بكلمة \'خالص\' إلا إذا كانت من نوع واحد مع نسبة شوائب لا تزيد عن 2.5%. المنتجات متعددة الألياف تحتوي على بيانات جميع الألياف ونسبها تنازلياً، مع تفاوت مسموح 5%.", "source": "TR-Textile-Products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc14_p008_c001", "title": "المادة (4) مكمل: المنتجات التي تحتوي على أجزاء غير نسيجية من أصل حيواني يجب أن ي", "content": "المادة (4) مكمل: المنتجات التي تحتوي على أجزاء غير نسيجية من أصل حيواني يجب أن يُكتب عليها \'يحتوي على أجزاء غير نسيجية من أصل حيواني\'. بطاقات البيانات: بالنسبة للألياف تلصق على التغليف؛ للخيوط تلصق على كل بكرة؛ للأقمشة تثبت على التغليف وجزء من اللفة؛ للملابس تربط أو تخاط بإحكام مع بيانات المقاسات؛ للسجاد تثبت بالخلف. البيانات باللغة العربية (ويجوز إضافة لغة أخرى). لا تحتوي على آيات قرآنية أو لفظ الجلالة. تتضمن: أنواع الألياف ونسبها، الوزن/المقاس/الأبعاد، اسم المورد وسجله التجاري، بلد المنشأ، نوع المعالجة، رموز العناية بالمنتج (الغسيل والتنظيف وإعادة التدوير).", "source": "TR-Textile-Products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc14_p009_c001", "title": "المادة (5) إجراءات سلامة المنتج النسيجي: يجب أن تستوفي المنتجات متطلبات السلامة ", "content": "المادة (5) إجراءات سلامة المنتج النسيجي: يجب أن تستوفي المنتجات متطلبات السلامة وصحة المستهلك والبيئة من: أضرار إكسسوارات ملابس الأطفال (الأزرار والحبال/الخيوط) – وفقاً للملحق (1). أضرار المواد المقاومة للحريق والانبعاثات السامة (إذا أقر المنتج بأنه مقاوم للاشتعال). أضرار المواد والمركبات الكيميائية أثناء الاستعمال والصيانة والتنظيف. أضرار تلوث مواد الحشو (الريش والزغب). الاختبارات: تحديد الرقم الهيدروجيني (pH) ضمن الحدود الآمنة. ثبات اللون للغسيل والعرق والاحتكاك (ولملابس الأطفال ثبات اللعاب). المواد الكيميائية الخطرة: CMR (مسرطنة/مطفرة/سامة للتكاثر)، PBT/vPvB (ثابتة/متراكمة/سامة)، ومواد خطير", "source": "TR-Textile-Products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc14_p010_c001", "title": "المادة (6) إجراءات تقويم المطابقة: 6/1 يجب على المورد (ملابس الأطفال دون 36 شهرا", "content": "المادة (6) إجراءات تقويم المطابقة: 6/1 يجب على المورد (ملابس الأطفال دون 36 شهراً والملابس الداخلية) الحصول على شهادة مطابقة Type 3 من جهة مقبولة (وفقاً ISO/IEC 17067، الملحق 7). 6/2 يجب على المورد (بقية المنتجات) الحصول على شهادة مطابقة Type 1a (الملحق 8). 6/3 تنفذ الجهة المقبولة الإجراءات حسب النموذج المحدد. 6/4 يُرفق ملف فني: إقرار المورد باملطابقة (الملحق 9)، تقارير المختبر لسلامة المنتج من المواد الكيماوية الخطرة. 6/5 المورد يتعاون مع الجهات الرقابية. 6/6 المنتج الحاصل على عالمة الجودة السعودية أو ما يعادلها يعتبر مطابقاً.", "source": "TR-Textile-Products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc14_p011_c001", "title": "المادة (7) مسؤوليات الجهات الرقابية (المنافذ والمصانع): التحقق من استيفاء المنتج", "content": "المادة (7) مسؤوليات الجهات الرقابية (المنافذ والمصانع): التحقق من استيفاء المنتجات لإجراءات تقويم المطابقة والوثائق الفنية. سحب عينات عشوائية وإحالتها للمختبرات. تحميل المستوردين تكاليف الاختبارات. سحب المنتجات غير المطابقة واتخاذ الإجراءات النظامية.", "source": "TR-Textile-Products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc14_p011_c002", "title": "المادة (8) مسؤوليات سلطات مسح السوق: تطبيق إجراءات مسح السوق على المنتجات في الأ", "content": "المادة (8) مسؤوليات سلطات مسح السوق: تطبيق إجراءات مسح السوق على المنتجات في الأسواق والمستودعات. سحب العينات وإجراء الاختبارات. عند عدم المطابقة، اتخاذ إجراءات السحب والاستدعاء وتطبيق عقوبات المادة (9).", "source": "TR-Textile-Products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc14_p012_c001", "title": "المادة (9) المخالفات والعقوبات: يُحظر صناعة واستيراد وعرض المنتجات غير المطابقة.", "content": "المادة (9) المخالفات والعقوبات: يُحظر صناعة واستيراد وعرض المنتجات غير المطابقة. عدم الاستيفاء يعتبر سبباً كافياً للحكم بعدم المطابقة في حالات: عدم تثبيت بطاقات البيانات، عدم اكتمال البيانات أو إرشادات السلامة، عدم إصدار شهادة المطابقة أو إقرار المورد، عدم توفر الوثائق الفنية. الإجراءات: سحب المنتج من المستودعات أو السوق لتصحيح المخالفة أو إعادة تصديره أو إتلافه. سحب المنتجات أو حجزها أو إتلافها أو استدعائها من الأسواق على نفقة الجهة المخالفة. الهيئة تلغي شهادة المطابقة. يعاقب المخالف بعقوبات نظام مكافحة الغش التجاري.", "source": "TR-Textile-Products.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p001_c001", "title": "Saudi Arabia SASO certification scheme. TÜV SÜD | GMA Saudi Arabia for textiles ", "content": "Saudi Arabia SASO certification scheme. TÜV SÜD | GMA Saudi Arabia for textiles products. 30 October 2019.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p002_c001", "title": "Meet the speakers: Mr. Angelo Polizzi (Global Head, Global Market Access), Mrs. ", "content": "Meet the speakers: Mr. Angelo Polizzi (Global Head, Global Market Access), Mrs. Raffaella Santoro (Director, Global Strategic Solutions for Softlines), Eng. Ossama Khalil (Technical Manager, Product Services Division).", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p003_c001", "title": "TÜV SÜD facts: 150+ years, 1,000+ locations worldwide, €2.4 billion annual reven", "content": "TÜV SÜD facts: 150+ years, 1,000+ locations worldwide, €2.4 billion annual revenue, 42% revenue outside Germany, 574,000 certificates.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p004_c001", "title": "Product categories (consumer products) – includes textiles, clothing, accessorie", "content": "Product categories (consumer products) – includes textiles, clothing, accessories, footwear, leather goods, toys, childcare articles, sporting goods, etc.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p005_c001", "title": "Our expertise worldwide: Many countries have multiple locations for testing, ins", "content": "Our expertise worldwide: Many countries have multiple locations for testing, inspection & audit.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p006_c001", "title": "End-to-end solutions for entire business lifecycle: TESTING AND PRODUCT CERTIFIC", "content": "End-to-end solutions for entire business lifecycle: TESTING AND PRODUCT CERTIFICATION, INSPECTION, AUDITING AND SYSTEM CERTIFICATION, KNOWLEDGE SERVICES, TRAINING.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p007_c001", "title": "What is Global Market Access? Market access is the process of determining applic", "content": "What is Global Market Access? Market access is the process of determining applicable regulations and managing product compliance to access global markets. TÜV SÜD has dedicated Global Market Access (GMA) team.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p010_c001", "title": "GMA Top Solutions: Argentina, Australia, Belarus, Brazil, Canada, Cambodia, Chil", "content": "GMA Top Solutions: Argentina, Australia, Belarus, Brazil, Canada, Cambodia, Chile, China, Ecuador, Egypt, EAEU, GCC, India, Israel, Indonesia, Japan, Malaysia, Mexico, Mongolia, New Zealand, Philippines, Singapore, Thailand, Saudi Arabia, South Africa, South Korea, Taiwan, UAE, USA, Ukraine, Vietnam. GMA Solution for Softlines: Egypt, EAEU, Saudi Arabia, South Korea, Greater China.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p011_c001", "title": "General introduction: Saudi Arabia – largest economy in Arab world and Middle Ea", "content": "General introduction: Saudi Arabia – largest economy in Arab world and Middle East; top 20 economies worldwide; largest petroleum exporter; Saudi Vision 2030 launched in 2016 to reduce oil dependency and diversify economy.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p012_c001", "title": "Import in Saudi Arabia of Fashion products – graphic showing import trends.", "content": "Import in Saudi Arabia of Fashion products – graphic showing import trends.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p013_c001", "title": "SASO CoC vs SALEEM. CoC: Since 2004, Ministry of Commerce issued decree 6386 req", "content": "SASO CoC vs SALEEM. CoC: Since 2004, Ministry of Commerce issued decree 6386 requiring CoC for all consumer products. Since 1 April 2019, SABER/SALEEM replaced CoC program. Products classified into regulated and non-regulated based on risk level.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p014_c001", "title": "Difference between CoC and SALEEM: CoC initiated by importer/exporter, each ship", "content": "Difference between CoC and SALEEM: CoC initiated by importer/exporter, each shipment has CoC, no mandatory factory audit, no shipment inspection, hard copy certificate. SALEEM: real importer via SABER registration; PCoC (valid 1 year) + SCoC per shipment; factory audit mandatory for Type 3 (children\'s products and underwear); e-certificate via SABER platform involving importers, notified bodies, Saudi Customs.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p015_c001", "title": "Regulated products under SABER (by early 2019-2020): LVE, Toys, Lubricants, LPG ", "content": "Regulated products under SABER (by early 2019-2020): LVE, Toys, Lubricants, LPG appliances, Building Materials (steel, concrete, cement, sanitary ware, pipes), Elevators, Electric Scooters, Biodegradable Plastic Products, Electric batteries, Truck barriers, Paints and varnishes, Textile and apparel (including underwear for adults and children).", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p016_c001", "title": "Documents for imported goods customs clearance in Saudi Arabia: Conformity Certi", "content": "Documents for imported goods customs clearance in Saudi Arabia: Conformity Certificate required. Authorities may take random samples from imported consignments to verify compliance. If shipment arrives without CoC, it requires testing by an approved local laboratory.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p017_c001", "title": "Application documents: Application for Certification; Declaration of Conformity ", "content": "Application documents: Application for Certification; Declaration of Conformity (printed on applicant\'s letterhead, signed and stamped); Latest Test Reports from ISO 17025 accredited lab complying with SASO requirements; Trade license; Actual product photos, marking and label.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p018_c001", "title": "SASO CoC process flowchart: Application -> Document Review -> Testing (if needed", "content": "SASO CoC process flowchart: Application -> Document Review -> Testing (if needed) -> Certificate Issuance. TAT 3-4 days.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p020_c001", "title": "SALEEM implementation: On 24 August 2018, SASO published Official Gazette for Te", "content": "SALEEM implementation: On 24 August 2018, SASO published Official Gazette for Technical Regulation of Textile Products 02-05-18-164 M.A. Textile products mandatory to register with SABER on 1 December 2019.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p021_c001", "title": "HS codes under textile technical regulation: 5001-5007 (silk), 5101-5113 (wool),", "content": "HS codes under textile technical regulation: 5001-5007 (silk), 5101-5113 (wool), 5201-5212 (cotton), 5301-5311 (other natural vegetable fibers like linen, hemp), 5401-5408 (nylon and polyamides), 5501-5516 (polyethylene and polyesters), 5601-5609 (wadding, felt, special yarns, ropes), 5701-5705 (rugs and carpets), 5801-5811 (woven pile fabrics, printed badges, gowns, ribbons), 5901-5911 (textile fabrics coated with gum), 6001-6009 (pile fabrics knitted), 6101-6117 (knitted apparel), 6201-6217 (non-knitted apparel), 6301-6310 (other made-up textile articles, sets, rags), 6501-6505 (headgear), 6", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p023_c001", "title": "SALEEM certification stages for textiles: Stage 1: Importer Registration & appli", "content": "SALEEM certification stages for textiles: Stage 1: Importer Registration & application to TÜV SÜD Middle East. Stage 2: Products registration according to fiber composition. Stage 3: Product certificate request and issuance. Stage 4: Shipment certificate request and issuance based on invoice.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p024_c001", "title": "Application documents for textile SALEEM: Application for Certification; DoC; La", "content": "Application documents for textile SALEEM: Application for Certification; DoC; Latest test reports from ISO 17025 lab; ISO 14001 certificate of manufacturer; Trade license; Product photos, marking, label. If factory audit needed, factory location and ISO 14001 required.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p026_c001", "title": "Conformity assessment procedure for textiles: Suppliers must obtain CoC from not", "content": "Conformity assessment procedure for textiles: Suppliers must obtain CoC from notified body: Type 1A for most textile products; Type 3 (with audit) for children\'s products and underwear. Audit includes manufacturing site audit for regulated products.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p027_c001", "title": "Audit requirements for Type 3 (Article 3.3-3.4): System documentation must inclu", "content": "Audit requirements for Type 3 (Article 3.3-3.4): System documentation must include quality objectives, organizational structure, manufacturing techniques, inspections and tests, records (test/calibration reports, personnel qualifications), control methods. Notified Body evaluates system for three years.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p030_c001", "title": "Labelling Requirements for textiles: Information must be easily legible, clear, ", "content": "Labelling Requirements for textiles: Information must be easily legible, clear, uniform in size/style/font, written in Arabic or Arabic+English, inerasable, easy to read before purchase (including e-commerce). External packing must have: supplier name/commercial registration, manufacturer/importer name/trademark, size, product name. Product label/hangtag: fiber composition, country of origin, product name/importer name/trademark, size. Care instruction label: washing, bleaching, drying, ironing instructions, precautions, care symbols.", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc15_p031_c001", "title": "Testing parameters for textile products: Drawstrings on children\'s clothing (SAS", "content": "Testing parameters for textile products: Drawstrings on children\'s clothing (SASO EN 14682), Care labelling symbol (SASO-ISO-3758), pH (SASO ISO 3071), Colour fastness (SASO-GSO-1268), Formaldehyde (SASO-ISO 14184-1&2), Chlorophenol (Textile: XP G08-015, Leather: SASO-ISO 17070), Extractable Heavy Metal, Azo Dyes, Carcinogenic Dyes, Allergenic Dyes, Flame retardants (SASO-ISO 17881-1&2), Pesticides, Phthalates (SASO-ISO 14389), Organotin compounds (SASO-ISO 17353).", "source": "tuv-sud-SASO.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p001_c001", "title": "UNDERSTANDING TEXTILE IMPORTS TO SAUDI ARABIA. The Essential Guide to Conformity", "content": "UNDERSTANDING TEXTILE IMPORTS TO SAUDI ARABIA. The Essential Guide to Conformity Assessment for textile imports in Saudi Arabia. www.exporting-to-saudi.com", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p002_c001", "title": "DISCLAIMER: Data herein is for information purposes only and represents opinion ", "content": "DISCLAIMER: Data herein is for information purposes only and represents opinion and analysis of author at time of publication. Author neither confirms nor guarantees exhaustiveness/accuracy.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p003_c001", "title": "Contents: 1. Introduction; 2. Textile Trade Statistics; 3. Product Standards for", "content": "Contents: 1. Introduction; 2. Textile Trade Statistics; 3. Product Standards for Textile Imports into Saudi Arabia; 4. Documentation Requirements; 5. Technical Requirements; 6. Importing & Exporting Process; 7. Case Study; 8. Appendix.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p004_c001", "title": "1. INTRODUCTION: Saudi Arabia is largest economy in MENA region, population >34 ", "content": "1. INTRODUCTION: Saudi Arabia is largest economy in MENA region, population >34 million. Imports significant textiles and clothing. Importers must comply with stringent regulations before importing textile products.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p005_c001", "title": "2. TEXTILE TRADE STATISTICS. Global textile trade valued over $700 billion in 20", "content": "2. TEXTILE TRADE STATISTICS. Global textile trade valued over $700 billion in 2020. Top importers: USA, Germany, Japan. Saudi Arabia imported $8.05B in textiles in 2021, becoming 27th largest importer. Textile products were 7th most imported products in Saudi Arabia.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p005_c002", "title": "Saudi Arabian Textile Import Market: From 2018-2021, market grew at average annu", "content": "Saudi Arabian Textile Import Market: From 2018-2021, market grew at average annual rate 13-15%, reaching over $8B. Growth driven by increasing demand, retail expansion, consumer awareness of quality/safety standards.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p006_c001", "title": "Saudi Arabia textile market growth graph (2016-2021).", "content": "Saudi Arabia textile market growth graph (2016-2021).", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p007_c001", "title": "Saudi Arabia imports textiles primarily from: China (largest), UAE, India, Bangl", "content": "Saudi Arabia imports textiles primarily from: China (largest), UAE, India, Bangladesh, Hong Kong. Emerging exporters: Vietnam, Ethiopia.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p008_c001", "title": "Top textile products exported to Saudi Arabia in 2020 (HS codes 61 & 62): knitte", "content": "Top textile products exported to Saudi Arabia in 2020 (HS codes 61 & 62): knitted/crocheted apparel, non-knitted apparel, clothing accessories.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p009_c001", "title": "3. PRODUCT STANDARDS FOR TEXTILE IMPORTS. SASO responsible for developing and en", "content": "3. PRODUCT STANDARDS FOR TEXTILE IMPORTS. SASO responsible for developing and enforcing standards. All textile imports must comply with SASO technical regulations to ensure quality and safety.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p010_c001", "title": "Textile Products Safety Regulations (TPSR) sets safety requirements: chemical pr", "content": "Textile Products Safety Regulations (TPSR) sets safety requirements: chemical properties (formaldehyde, heavy metals, azo dyes limits); physical properties (strength, durability, colorfastness); labeling requirements (product name, fiber content, country of origin, care instructions); testing methods (colorfastness, shrinkage, flammability).", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p011_c001", "title": "Labeling regulations (TPLR) require: types of fibers with mass percentages; weig", "content": "Labeling regulations (TPLR) require: types of fibers with mass percentages; weight/size/dimensions; supplier name and commercial register on external packaging; country of origin; washing/cleaning guidelines and symbols; labels shall not contain Quranic verses or the word \'Allah\'; labels tightly fixed, difficult to remove; information in Arabic or Arabic+English in indelible manner.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p012_c001", "title": "Chemical requirements: limits for Formaldehyde, Pentachlorophenol (PCP), Tetrach", "content": "Chemical requirements: limits for Formaldehyde, Pentachlorophenol (PCP), Tetrachlorophenol (TeCP), Ortho-Phenylphenol (OPP); Heavy Metals (Antimony, Arsenic, Lead, Cadmium, Mercury, Copper, Total Chromium VI, Cobalt, Nickel); Carcinogenic Amines in Azo Dyes; Flame Retardants; Insecticides, Herbicides, Fungicides; Chlorinated Compounds; Phthalates; Organotin Compounds; pH value; Color stability tests (washing, perspiration, friction, and for children\'s clothing: saliva).", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p012_c002", "title": "Note: Products with ecological badge or equivalent from SASO-approved bodies dee", "content": "Note: Products with ecological badge or equivalent from SASO-approved bodies deemed in conformity without need for conformity assessment or factory audit after verifying certificate validity and compliance to SASO standards.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p013_c001", "title": "4. DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS: Commercial Registration and Investment License; C", "content": "4. DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS: Commercial Registration and Investment License; Certificate of Conformity (CoC) from notified third-party body; Commercial Invoice (price, quantity, description); Bill of Lading (exporter/importer info, shipping date, port); Packing List (# packages, weight, dimensions).", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p014_c001", "title": "5. TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS: Definitions of Technical Regulation, Standard, Essent", "content": "5. TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS: Definitions of Technical Regulation, Standard, Essential Requirements, Market Surveillance, Regulatory Authorities, Hazard(s), Risk(s), Supplier, Conformity Assessment Procedures, Notified Bodies, Certificate of Conformity, Supplier Declaration of Conformity, Saudi Quality Mark, Placing on Market, Display in Market, Withdrawal, Recall.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p015_c001", "title": "All textile products under scope must comply with applicable SASO/GSO/internatio", "content": "All textile products under scope must comply with applicable SASO/GSO/international standards listed in annex. Required certification scheme: Type 3 for children\'s products and underwear; Type 1a for all other textile products.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p016_c001", "title": "6. IMPORTING & EXPORTING PROCESS. Importing to Saudi Arabia: 1) Obtain Commercia", "content": "6. IMPORTING & EXPORTING PROCESS. Importing to Saudi Arabia: 1) Obtain Commercial Registration and Investment License; 2) Ensure compliance and obtain certifications; 3) Arrange shipment; 4) Pay import duties/taxes; 5) Submit documentation to Saudi customs; 6) Distribute/sell.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p017_c001", "title": "Exporting from Saudi Arabia: 1) Obtain export license; 2) Ensure compliance and ", "content": "Exporting from Saudi Arabia: 1) Obtain export license; 2) Ensure compliance and obtain certifications; 3) Comply with marking (SASO ISO 3758); 4) Ensure customs documentation; 5) Pay export duties; 6) Arrange shipping.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p018_c001", "title": "Cotecna SASO/SABER certification: Two-stage process – PCoC (Product Certificate ", "content": "Cotecna SASO/SABER certification: Two-stage process – PCoC (Product Certificate of Conformity, valid 1 year) and SCoC (Shipment Certificate per consignment). Steps: Importer registers on SABER; selects Cotecna as CB; Cotecna guides product registration; uploads documentation; checks and schedules testing/audit; issues PCoC; then SCoC per shipment.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p020_c001", "title": "7. CASE STUDY: Ensuring legitimacy of textile goods (in collaboration with Wimpe", "content": "7. CASE STUDY: Ensuring legitimacy of textile goods (in collaboration with Wimpey Laboratories). Physical defects (seam puckering, open/broken seams, discoloration, holes) and chemical-related defects (flame retardants, restricted dyes).", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p021_c001", "title": "Background: Target severed ties with Welspun India in 2016 for mislabeling Egypt", "content": "Background: Target severed ties with Welspun India in 2016 for mislabeling Egyptian cotton. Cotton Egypt Association estimated 90% of global Egyptian cotton supplies in 2020 were fake. GOTS opened investigation on 20,000 tons of Indian cotton incorrectly certified as organic.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p022_c001", "title": "Role of Cotecna Group: offers inspection and testing tailored to textile product", "content": "Role of Cotecna Group: offers inspection and testing tailored to textile products using SASO 277T (Color Fastness to Water, Rubbing, Perspiration). Process: sample collection, testing protocols, analysis, authentication report.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p023_c001", "title": "Physical defects classification: quality defects, fabric defects, garment defect", "content": "Physical defects classification: quality defects, fabric defects, garment defects (faulty zippers, irregular hemming, loose buttons, raw edges, improper buttonholes, uneven parts, color differences). Chemical defects: Azo dyes (60-70% of fabric colorants), Flame retardants (required for children\'s clothing), Phthalates (found in 3 products noncompliant), Heavy metals (lead, chromium – 2 products exceeded limits).", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p024_c001", "title": "Specific observations in case study: Seam puckering (gathering of seam), Open or", "content": "Specific observations in case study: Seam puckering (gathering of seam), Open or broken seam (portion not covered by thread), Broken stitch (non-continuous thread), Drop stitch/skipped stitch (irregular stitching), Uncut/loose thread (extra threads on seam line), Distorted knitting.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p025_c001", "title": "Industry strategy and garment durability: WRAP\'s Sustainable Clothing Action Pla", "content": "Industry strategy and garment durability: WRAP\'s Sustainable Clothing Action Plan (2012) engaged retailers on garment longevity. Survey found most prevalent issues: pilling (55%), color fading (53%), fabric breakdown (29%), accidental damage (29%), loss of dimensional stability (20%), logo failure (16%), discoloration (15%), holes in seam (14%), trim failure (8%).", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p027_c001", "title": "CONCLUSION: Import of textile products to Saudi Arabia subject to stringent SASO", "content": "CONCLUSION: Import of textile products to Saudi Arabia subject to stringent SASO regulations covering chemical/physical properties, labeling, testing, technical specifications. Cotecna helps importers navigate compliance.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p028_c001", "title": "More about SASO: government body entrusted with standards, measurements, quality", "content": "More about SASO: government body entrusted with standards, measurements, quality. Provides quality control measures, sets conformity procedures, protects consumers from substandard/counterfeit goods.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p029_c001", "title": "More about Cotecna: leading TIC provider, notified by SASO to issue CoC for regu", "content": "More about Cotecna: leading TIC provider, notified by SASO to issue CoC for regulated products to KSA.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p030_c001", "title": "More about Wimpey Laboratories: ISO/IEC 17025 accredited lab, ISO 9001/14001/450", "content": "More about Wimpey Laboratories: ISO/IEC 17025 accredited lab, ISO 9001/14001/45001 certified, provides testing and calibration services globally.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc16_p031_c001", "title": "REFERENCES: Trading Economics, Fitch Solutions, Zimstat, Global Edge, Volza, Tri", "content": "REFERENCES: Trading Economics, Fitch Solutions, Zimstat, Global Edge, Volza, Tridge, OEC, Comtrade, Yumpu, Drinks Int, Tilasto, Mordor Intelligence, WITS Worldbank, Kohan Textile Journal.", "source": "voc-saudi-textile-whitepaper-final.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p001_c001", "title": "MAKING REGIONAL INTEGRATION WORK. Company perspectives on non-tariff measures in", "content": "MAKING REGIONAL INTEGRATION WORK. Company perspectives on non-tariff measures in Arab States. International Trade Centre (ITC) publication, 2015.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p004_c001", "title": "FOREWORD. Deeper regional integration is important for SMEs. Arab region has mad", "content": "FOREWORD. Deeper regional integration is important for SMEs. Arab region has made integration a priority but intra-Arab trade remains low compared to other regions. ITC enterprise-level analysis of four economies (Egypt, Morocco, State of Palestine, Tunisia) provides insight into day-to-day challenges. NTMs and regional market regulation compliance are examined. Market access begins at home.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p005_c001", "title": "ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS. Publication written by Ursula Hermelink and Mathieu Loridan ba", "content": "ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS. Publication written by Ursula Hermelink and Mathieu Loridan based on ITC NTM surveys in Egypt, Morocco, State of Palestine, Tunisia. Financial support from UK DFID, Government of Canada, USAID, ITFC.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p007_c001", "title": "CONTENTS: Chapter 1 Regional Overview; Chapter 2 NTM Survey Findings; Chapter 3 ", "content": "CONTENTS: Chapter 1 Regional Overview; Chapter 2 NTM Survey Findings; Chapter 3 Product Quality and Conformity; Chapter 4 Rules of Origin and Other Trade-Related Measures; Chapter 5 Customs Clearance and Border Controls; Chapter 6 Conclusions and Recommendations.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p008_c001", "title": "EXECUTIVE SUMMARY. Regional integration has improved business prospects. Tariffs", "content": "EXECUTIVE SUMMARY. Regional integration has improved business prospects. Tariffs eliminated, but non-tariff measures (NTMs) keep markets fragmented. Intra-Arab trade low compared to other regions. ITC surveys in Egypt, Morocco, Palestine, Tunisia identify bottlenecks. 44% of trading companies reported facing burdensome NTMs. Procedural obstacles increase compliance costs. Recommendations: transparency, harmonization, streamlining customs, making existing agreements work.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p011_c001", "title": "CHAPTER 1: REGIONAL OVERVIEW. Overlapping preferential agreements (GAFTA, Agadir", "content": "CHAPTER 1: REGIONAL OVERVIEW. Overlapping preferential agreements (GAFTA, Agadir, COMESA, bilateral) but integration modest. Tariff preferences have not translated into integration. NTMs now the main obstacle. Surveys point to intraregional trade obstacles.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p012_c001", "title": "Figure 1: Trade agreements involving Arab States (map showing overlapping agreem", "content": "Figure 1: Trade agreements involving Arab States (map showing overlapping agreements).", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p018_c001", "title": "CHAPTER 2: NTM SURVEY FINDINGS IN ARAB STATES. 44% of trading companies faced bu", "content": "CHAPTER 2: NTM SURVEY FINDINGS IN ARAB STATES. 44% of trading companies faced burdensome NTMs. 24% (agriculture) and 21% (manufacturing) of burdensome measures applied by home country. Arab States responsible for disproportionate share of reported cases relative to export share. For manufacturing: 47% of NTM cases concern Arab States\' regulations vs only 16% of exports.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p019_c001", "title": "Figure 3: Breakdown of burdensome NTM cases reported by exporters. Figure 4: Bur", "content": "Figure 3: Breakdown of burdensome NTM cases reported by exporters. Figure 4: Burdensome NTM cases vs export share. Shows Arab States more difficult to access than EU relative to trade volume.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p020_c001", "title": "Figure 5: Agricultural exports – burdensome NTMs applied by partner countries. 5", "content": "Figure 5: Agricultural exports – burdensome NTMs applied by partner countries. 54% SPS/TBT, 38% conformity assessment, 31% rules of origin. Figure 6: Manufacturing exports – 31% rules of origin for Arab partners vs much lower for non-Arab.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p021_c001", "title": "Figure 7: Burdensome NTMs applied at home – export inspections (20% for agricult", "content": "Figure 7: Burdensome NTMs applied at home – export inspections (20% for agriculture), certification, taxes, licensing. Figure 8: Why exporters find NTMs a burden – procedural obstacles account for 61% (agriculture) and 94% (manufacturing) of home-applied measures. This suggests many obstacles could be eliminated by tackling procedures rather than changing rules.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p022_c001", "title": "Table 2: Procedural obstacles affecting exports – customs most frequently mentio", "content": "Table 2: Procedural obstacles affecting exports – customs most frequently mentioned, then testing/certification agencies. Delays, lack of facilities, administrative burdens, high costs. Table 3: Technical NTM-related procedural obstacles.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p025_c001", "title": "CHAPTER 3: PRODUCT QUALITY AND CONFORMITY. Compliance challenges with technical ", "content": "CHAPTER 3: PRODUCT QUALITY AND CONFORMITY. Compliance challenges with technical regulations: strict environmental standards, product safety measures, traceability requirements. Labelling issues stand out: frequent changes, differing requirements between countries (date formats, language, stickers vs engraving). Fines up to $5,000 per shipment for non-compliance.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p026_c001", "title": "Product testing and certification issues: lengthy procedures (30-60 days), frequ", "content": "Product testing and certification issues: lengthy procedures (30-60 days), frequent renewal, excessive paperwork, insufficient/absent laboratory infrastructure, high certification costs (e.g., $4,000+ per shipment for EN 817 certification). Lack of recognition of certificates despite mutual recognition agreements. Lack of transparency of foreign standards.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p027_c001", "title": "Product registration and import authorization: procedures perceived as very stri", "content": "Product registration and import authorization: procedures perceived as very strict, especially in Gulf countries. Delays exceeding one year, need to re-register annually or biennially, costs up to $2,850 per product. Even after registration, products held up at border for verification.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p029_c001", "title": "CHAPTER 4: RULES OF ORIGIN AND OTHER TRADE-RELATED MEASURES. Rules of origin maj", "content": "CHAPTER 4: RULES OF ORIGIN AND OTHER TRADE-RELATED MEASURES. Rules of origin major challenge: preferential treatment not granted de facto despite GAFTA. Language issues (100% Arabic certificates required). Inefficiency in issuing certificates (2 days to 3 months). \'Made in Palestine\' issues: suspect Israeli inputs, refusal of preferential treatment, extra documentation.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p030_c001", "title": "Other trade-related measures: terms of payment (letters of credit required by so", "content": "Other trade-related measures: terms of payment (letters of credit required by some countries – delays up to 2 years); consular fees ($35+ per document); reference pricing and product reclassification; quantity controls (quotas, import bans) perceived as protectionism. \'Home-made\' problems: export permits, registration, taxes; lack of port security; poor transport infrastructure; bribes; lack of computerized processes.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p035_c001", "title": "CHAPTER 5: CUSTOMS CLEARANCE AND BORDER CONTROLS. Infrastructure challenges: out", "content": "CHAPTER 5: CUSTOMS CLEARANCE AND BORDER CONTROLS. Infrastructure challenges: outdated scanners, missing storage facilities (especially cooling). Personnel issues: limited service hours, staff shortages, poorly trained inspectors causing product damage. Lack of transparency: frequently changing procedures, inadequate dissemination. Lack of coordination between agencies and between countries. Result: lengthy (days to weeks), bureaucratic, costly clearance (inspection charges $200+, bribes $85/truck).", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p038_c001", "title": "Figure 12: Burdensome inspection requirements applied by Arab States.", "content": "Figure 12: Burdensome inspection requirements applied by Arab States.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p041_c001", "title": "CHAPTER 6: CONCLUSIONS AND RECOMMENDATIONS. Key messages: Market access begins a", "content": "CHAPTER 6: CONCLUSIONS AND RECOMMENDATIONS. Key messages: Market access begins at home. Make existing agreements work (GAFTA, mutual recognition, Kyoto Convention, Trade Facilitation Agreement). Transparency is pivotal. Most obstacles are procedural, not due to strictness of regulations.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p042_c001", "title": "Recommendation – Transparency: Publish official deadlines and response times. Ad", "content": "Recommendation – Transparency: Publish official deadlines and response times. Adopt tracking system for requests. Establish regional trade information portal. Create regional export guides (labelling, traceability, quality standards, customs procedures). Increase regional business matchmaking. Train private/public sector on trade agreements. Enhance TISI advisory services for SMEs.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p043_c001", "title": "Recommendation – Quality and Conformity: Identify priority sectors. Harmonize st", "content": "Recommendation – Quality and Conformity: Identify priority sectors. Harmonize standards and technical requirements. Harmonize labelling requirements (standardized \'Arab label\' in Arabic/French/English). Conformity assessment: map testing needs, designate reference laboratories, ensure mutual recognition, create sustainable financial mechanisms for SMEs to afford testing.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p044_c001", "title": "Recommendation – Trade-related measures: Invest in people and trade support infr", "content": "Recommendation – Trade-related measures: Invest in people and trade support infrastructure (electronic document submission, fast-track for repeat exporters). Institutionalize ongoing public-private dialogue (national trade facilitation committees). Strengthen TISIs. Address wider business environment (SME access to trade finance, transport infrastructure). Create trade obstacles alert system. Clarify and harmonize rules of origin. Work towards Arab customs union.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-doc17_p045_c001", "title": "Recommendation – Customs and border controls: Review customs legislation. Streng", "content": "Recommendation – Customs and border controls: Review customs legislation. Strengthen risk analysis to avoid 100% inspections. Provide necessary storage infrastructure. Institutionalize joint border controls. Apply ICTs: modern detection technologies, electronic copies (\'paperless clearance\'), single window. Strengthen partnerships and information exchange. Increase staff and institutionalize training. Initiate culture change – customs as \'welcome point\'.", "source": "workingtowardsregionalintegrationwebpdf.pdf", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0000", "title": "【A.适用范围与定义】 [适用范围] 本法规适用于在沙特市场上展示的所有纺织产品，包括含至少80%重量纺织纤维的产品（纤维、纺织纱线、窗帘、家具、地毯、服装、技", "content": "【A.适用范围与定义】 [适用范围] 本法规适用于在沙特市场上展示的所有纺织产品，包括含至少80%重量纺织纤维的产品（纤维、纺织纱线、窗帘、家具、地毯、服装、技术织物） (出处: SASO TR Art.2/1 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0001", "title": "【A.适用范围与定义】 [适用范围] 含至少80%重量纺织组件的家具（包括毯子、雨伞、遮阳篷）也适用本法规 (出处: SASO TR Art.2/2 | 严重程", "content": "【A.适用范围与定义】 [适用范围] 含至少80%重量纺织组件的家具（包括毯子、雨伞、遮阳篷）也适用本法规 (出处: SASO TR Art.2/2 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0002", "title": "【A.适用范围与定义】 [适用范围] 多层地板覆盖物的上层、所有床罩和床垫套、露营设备和产品的覆盖物（纺织组件≥80%）均在范围内 (出处: SASO TR A", "content": "【A.适用范围与定义】 [适用范围] 多层地板覆盖物的上层、所有床罩和床垫套、露营设备和产品的覆盖物（纺织组件≥80%）均在范围内 (出处: SASO TR Art.2/2 A-C | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0003", "title": "【A.适用范围与定义】 [适用范围] 与其他产品结合并构成其组成部分的纺织品（包括鞋类、箱包、头饰）也在范围内 (出处: SASO TR Art.2/2 D |", "content": "【A.适用范围与定义】 [适用范围] 与其他产品结合并构成其组成部分的纺织品（包括鞋类、箱包、头饰）也在范围内 (出处: SASO TR Art.2/2 D | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0004", "title": "【A.适用范围与定义】 [排除范围] 医疗用途的纺织品不适用本法规，归沙特食药监管局（SFDA）管辖 (出处: SASO TR Art.2 排除条款 | 严重程", "content": "【A.适用范围与定义】 [排除范围] 医疗用途的纺织品不适用本法规，归沙特食药监管局（SFDA）管辖 (出处: SASO TR Art.2 排除条款 | 严重程度: informational)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0005", "title": "【A.适用范围与定义】 [排除范围] 鞋类及配件适用单独的鞋类技术法规（SASO TR for Footwear），不适用纺织品法规 (出处: SASO TR ", "content": "【A.适用范围与定义】 [排除范围] 鞋类及配件适用单独的鞋类技术法规（SASO TR for Footwear），不适用纺织品法规 (出处: SASO TR Edition 2 (2024) | 严重程度: informational)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0006", "title": "【A.适用范围与定义】 [定义] 纺织产品定义：以原料或半原料形式组装或生产的，完全由纺织纤维组成的产品，无论混合或组装工艺如何 (出处: SASO TR Ar", "content": "【A.适用范围与定义】 [定义] 纺织产品定义：以原料或半原料形式组装或生产的，完全由纺织纤维组成的产品，无论混合或组装工艺如何 (出处: SASO TR Art.1 | 严重程度: informational)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0007", "title": "【A.适用范围与定义】 [定义] 纺织纤维定义：纺织工业原料的基本单位，具有柔韧性和柔软性，长度与横截面比率高，适合纺织应用。附录3列出49种国际认可的纤维名称", "content": "【A.适用范围与定义】 [定义] 纺织纤维定义：纺织工业原料的基本单位，具有柔韧性和柔软性，长度与横截面比率高，适合纺织应用。附录3列出49种国际认可的纤维名称 (出处: SASO TR Art.1 | 严重程度: informational)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0008", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-语言] 所有纺织品标签信息必须以阿拉伯语标注。2024年修订版已删除对英语的强制要求，仅保留阿拉伯语为必需语言，可额外使用其他语言 (", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-语言] 所有纺织品标签信息必须以阿拉伯语标注。2024年修订版已删除对英语的强制要求，仅保留阿拉伯语为必需语言，可额外使用其他语言 (出处: SASO TR Edition 2 (2024) / SGS Safeguards 7024 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0009", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-固定方式] 标签必须缝制或牢固固定在产品上，固定方式应符合纺织行业通用做法，不易移除 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 A", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-固定方式] 标签必须缝制或牢固固定在产品上，固定方式应符合纺织行业通用做法，不易移除 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 A-3 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0010", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-字体] 标签信息应使用清晰字体，大小和字体类型统一，消费者在购买时（包括网购）能轻松阅读 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-字体] 标签信息应使用清晰字体，大小和字体类型统一，消费者在购买时（包括网购）能轻松阅读 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 B | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0011", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-准确性] 标签和标记上的所有数据不得误导消费者，所有信息必须正确且经过验证 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 A-2, L", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-准确性] 标签和标记上的所有数据不得误导消费者，所有信息必须正确且经过验证 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 A-2, L-4 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0012", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-宗教禁忌] 标签不得包含古兰经经文或\'安拉\'一词，产品包装中的图像和文字不得违反沙特公共秩序、道德和伊斯兰价值观 (出处: SASO ", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-宗教禁忌] 标签不得包含古兰经经文或\'安拉\'一词，产品包装中的图像和文字不得违反沙特公共秩序、道德和伊斯兰价值观 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 L-5 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0013", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-纤维成分] 必须标注产品所含纤维的类型及质量百分比，按附录3中的标准名称标注，计算时需考虑附录4中的含湿率 (出处: SASO TR ", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-纤维成分] 必须标注产品所含纤维的类型及质量百分比，按附录3中的标准名称标注，计算时需考虑附录4中的含湿率 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 L-6 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0014", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-重量尺寸] 必须标注产品的重量、尺寸和尺寸信息 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 L-6 | 严重程度: mandator", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-重量尺寸] 必须标注产品的重量、尺寸和尺寸信息 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 L-6 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0015", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-供应商] 外包装上必须标注供应商名称及其商业注册号 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 L-6 | 严重程度: mandat", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-供应商] 外包装上必须标注供应商名称及其商业注册号 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 L-6 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0016", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-原产国] 必须标注原产国/制造国 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 L-6 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-原产国] 必须标注原产国/制造国 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 L-6 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0017", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-洗涤说明] 必须标注纺织品洗涤和清洁指南的信息和符号，确保产品安全，符号须符合相关标准（ISO 3758） (出处: SASO TR ", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-洗涤说明] 必须标注纺织品洗涤和清洁指南的信息和符号，确保产品安全，符号须符合相关标准（ISO 3758） (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 L-6 / SASO ISO 3758 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0018", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-品牌] 允许在标签上放置制造商的商标或品牌名称，但不得部分或全部包含所用纤维名称或可能误导消费者的名称 (出处: SASO TR Ar", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-品牌] 允许在标签上放置制造商的商标或品牌名称，但不得部分或全部包含所用纤维名称或可能误导消费者的名称 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 A-4 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0019", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-纯标注] 仅当产品完全由同一种纤维制成时才可标为\'纯\'或\'100%纯\'。厚毛织物杂质不超过5%，其他织物不超过2%（须为制造工艺需要，", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-纯标注] 仅当产品完全由同一种纤维制成时才可标为\'纯\'或\'100%纯\'。厚毛织物杂质不超过5%，其他织物不超过2%（须为制造工艺需要，非故意添加） (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 D | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0020", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-原毛标注] \'原毛(Raw Wool)\'标注仅限于未经任何纺纱和/或毡化加工、未经任何可能损坏原纤维的处理或使用的羊毛纤维 (出处: ", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-原毛标注] \'原毛(Raw Wool)\'标注仅限于未经任何纺纱和/或毡化加工、未经任何可能损坏原纤维的处理或使用的羊毛纤维 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 E | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0021", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-混纺] 多纤维纺织品须标注所有组成纤维的名称和重量百分比，按降序排列。主要纤维的允许公差为±5% (出处: SASO TR Art.4", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-混纺] 多纤维纺织品须标注所有组成纤维的名称和重量百分比，按降序排列。主要纤维的允许公差为±5% (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 F | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0022", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-混纺例外] 如某些纤维在制造过程中无法识别，同类纤维不超过总重5%或混合纤维不超过总重15%时，可标注为\'其他纤维\'并标明总百分比 (", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-混纺例外] 如某些纤维在制造过程中无法识别，同类纤维不超过总重5%或混合纤维不超过总重15%时，可标注为\'其他纤维\'并标明总百分比 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 F | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0023", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-装饰纤维] 纯装饰用纤维不超过成品重量7%、提供额外技术性能的纤维不超过成品重量2%时，不计入百分比 (出处: SASO TR Art", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-装饰纤维] 纯装饰用纤维不超过成品重量7%、提供额外技术性能的纤维不超过成品重量2%时，不计入百分比 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 G | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0024", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-多组件] 由两个或多个纤维成分不同的部件组成的产品，须标注每个组件的纤维成分。非主要衬里可豁免 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-多组件] 由两个或多个纤维成分不同的部件组成的产品，须标注每个组件的纤维成分。非主要衬里可豁免 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 H | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0025", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-动物源] 含有动物源非纺织部分的纺织品必须标注\'含有动物源非纺织部分\'，标注须清晰易懂且不误导消费者 (出处: SASO TR Art", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-动物源] 含有动物源非纺织部分的纺织品必须标注\'含有动物源非纺织部分\'，标注须清晰易懂且不误导消费者 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 I | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0026", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-地毯] 地毯和毛毯须添加技术特性和使用条件，信息须显示在牢固附着或粘贴在产品背面的标签上。清真寺地毯须适用相关SASO标准 (出处: ", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-地毯] 地毯和毛毯须添加技术特性和使用条件，信息须显示在牢固附着或粘贴在产品背面的标签上。清真寺地毯须适用相关SASO标准 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 J | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0027", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-纱线] 缝纫线须添加纱线号，标签须附在每个线轴上 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 J | 严重程度: mandatory", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-纱线] 缝纫线须添加纱线号，标签须附在每个线轴上 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 J | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0028", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-面料] 面料标签须附在包装上，且永久固定在卷筒的一部分上，使标签在商店中始终可见 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 J |", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-面料] 面料标签须附在包装上，且永久固定在卷筒的一部分上，使标签在商店中始终可见 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 J | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0029", "title": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-服装] 服装标签须牢固附着或缝在衣服上，须按相关标准添加服装编码数据 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 J | 严重程度:", "content": "【B.标签要求】 [标签-服装] 服装标签须牢固附着或缝在衣服上，须按相关标准添加服装编码数据 (出处: SASO TR Art.4/1/2 J | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0030", "title": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-pH] 儿童纺织品 pH 值范围：4.0 - 7.5 (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 1 |", "content": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-pH] 儿童纺织品 pH 值范围：4.0 - 7.5 (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 1 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0031", "title": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-pH] 直接接触皮肤的纺织品 pH 值范围：4.0 - 7.5 (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Tabl", "content": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-pH] 直接接触皮肤的纺织品 pH 值范围：4.0 - 7.5 (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 1 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0032", "title": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-pH] 不直接接触皮肤/装饰材料 pH 值范围：4.0 - 9.0 (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Ta", "content": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-pH] 不直接接触皮肤/装饰材料 pH 值范围：4.0 - 9.0 (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 1 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0033", "title": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-甲醛] 儿童产品甲醛含量：< 20 ppm（低于检测限） (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 2", "content": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-甲醛] 儿童产品甲醛含量：< 20 ppm（低于检测限） (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 2 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0034", "title": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-甲醛] 直接接触皮肤产品甲醛含量：≤ 75 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 2 | ", "content": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-甲醛] 直接接触皮肤产品甲醛含量：≤ 75 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 2 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0035", "title": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-甲醛] 不直接接触皮肤/装饰材料甲醛含量：≤ 300 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table", "content": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-甲醛] 不直接接触皮肤/装饰材料甲醛含量：≤ 300 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 2 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0036", "title": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-酚类] 五氯苯酚(PCP) — 儿童产品：≤ 0.05 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Tabl", "content": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-酚类] 五氯苯酚(PCP) — 儿童产品：≤ 0.05 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 3 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0037", "title": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-酚类] 五氯苯酚(PCP) — 直接接触皮肤/非直接接触：≤ 0.5 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex ", "content": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-酚类] 五氯苯酚(PCP) — 直接接触皮肤/非直接接触：≤ 0.5 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 3 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0038", "title": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-酚类] 四氯苯酚(TeCP) — 儿童产品：≤ 0.05 ppm；直接/非直接接触：≤ 0.5 ppm (出处: S", "content": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-酚类] 四氯苯酚(TeCP) — 儿童产品：≤ 0.05 ppm；直接/非直接接触：≤ 0.5 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 3 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0039", "title": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-酚类] 邻苯基苯酚(OPP) — 儿童产品：≤ 0.5 ppm；直接接触：≤ 1.0 ppm；非直接接触：≤ 1.0", "content": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-酚类] 邻苯基苯酚(OPP) — 儿童产品：≤ 0.5 ppm；直接接触：≤ 1.0 ppm；非直接接触：≤ 1.0 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 3 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0040", "title": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-酚类] 检测方法须使用 SASO ISO 17070（皮革）标准和与皮肤接触部分相关的分析标准 (出处: SASO ", "content": "【C.化学安全-甲醛pH酚类】 [化学安全-酚类] 检测方法须使用 SASO ISO 17070（皮革）标准和与皮肤接触部分相关的分析标准 (出处: SASO TR Art.5/2/3-2 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0041", "title": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-锑(Sb)] 锑(Sb) — 儿童产品：≤ 30 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 5 | 严", "content": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-锑(Sb)] 锑(Sb) — 儿童产品：≤ 30 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 5 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0042", "title": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-锑(Sb)] 锑(Sb) — 直接接触皮肤：≤ 30 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 5 |", "content": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-锑(Sb)] 锑(Sb) — 直接接触皮肤：≤ 30 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 5 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0043", "title": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-锑(Sb)] 锑(Sb) — 非直接接触皮肤：≤ 30 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 5 ", "content": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-锑(Sb)] 锑(Sb) — 非直接接触皮肤：≤ 30 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 5 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0044", "title": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-砷(As)] 砷(As) — 儿童产品：≤ 0.2 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 5 | ", "content": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-砷(As)] 砷(As) — 儿童产品：≤ 0.2 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 5 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0045", "title": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-砷(As)] 砷(As) — 直接/非直接接触皮肤：≤ 1.0 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Tabl", "content": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-砷(As)] 砷(As) — 直接/非直接接触皮肤：≤ 1.0 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 5 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0046", "title": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-铅(Pb)] 铅(Pb) — 儿童产品：≤ 0.2 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 5 | ", "content": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-铅(Pb)] 铅(Pb) — 儿童产品：≤ 0.2 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 5 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0047", "title": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-铅(Pb)] 铅(Pb) — 直接/非直接接触皮肤：≤ 1.0 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Tabl", "content": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-铅(Pb)] 铅(Pb) — 直接/非直接接触皮肤：≤ 1.0 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 5 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0048", "title": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-镉(Cd)] 镉(Cd) — 所有类别（儿童/直接/非直接接触）：≤ 0.1 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex ", "content": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-镉(Cd)] 镉(Cd) — 所有类别（儿童/直接/非直接接触）：≤ 0.1 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 5 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-rule_p001_c0049", "title": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-铬(Cr)] 总铬(Cr) — 儿童产品：≤ 1.0 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 5 |", "content": "【D.化学安全-重金属】 [重金属-铬(Cr)] 总铬(Cr) — 儿童产品：≤ 1.0 ppm (出处: SASO TR Annex 2, Table 5 | 严重程度: mandatory)", "source": "414_pieces_infor.json", "dimension": "compliance", "tags": []},
